🦆🌱☄️ GO — R6.99

👑 HORTUS CONSTITUTIONAL MIGRATION, COMPATIBILITY & SAFE TRANSITION PROTOCOL

R6.98 is frozen.

R6.98 established that the Constitution is a versioned, immutable governance state.

R6.99 now governs the dangerous interval between states.

The central question:

> How does a living Citadel move from constitutional state Cₙ to Cₙ₊₁ without creating an authority discontinuity, orphaned delegation, incompatible ELIXERS, or an unprovable transition?



The answer:

> A CONSTITUTIONAL TRANSITION IS ITSELF A GOVERNED, EVIDENCED, WATERMARKED STATE TRANSITION.



Not:

OLD CONSTITUTION
      ↓
UPDATE
      ↓
NEW CONSTITUTION

But:

Cₙ
 ↓
MIGRATION PLAN
 ↓
COMPATIBILITY ANALYSIS
 ↓
IMPACT ANALYSIS
 ↓
TRANSITION AUTHORITY
 ↓
PRE-CUTOVER STATE
 ↓
CUTOVER
 ↓
Cₙ₊₁
 ↓
POST-CUTOVER VERIFICATION
 ↓
REPLAY


---

I. 🔱 MIGRATION ≠ REPLACEMENT

A constitutional migration does not destroy Cₙ.

It establishes:

Cₙ
 ↓
TRANSITION
 ↓
Cₙ₊₁

with:

Cₙ = HISTORICAL GOVERNING STATE
Cₙ₊₁ = NEW GOVERNING STATE

Therefore:

> Migration changes future governance applicability; it does not erase historical governance.




---

II. 🌱 THE MIGRATION OBJECT

R6.99 introduces a first-class conceptual object:

ConstitutionalMigration

Containing:

migration_id

source_version
target_version

migration_authority

proposal_reference
evidence_reference

compatibility_result
impact_assessment

affected_authorities
affected_delegations
affected_elixers
affected_relations

transition_conditions

cutover_time
verification_window

rollback_policy
watermark

status

The exact implementation remains open.

The semantic requirement does not:

> A constitutional transition must itself be attributable and replayable.




---

III. 🧭 Z.A.N.D. — BEFORE MIGRATION

The first gate:

ASSUMPTION = NONE

Before Cₙ → Cₙ₊₁, PALACO must establish:

WHAT IS CHANGING?

WHY?

WHO IS AUTHORIZED TO CHANGE IT?

WHICH SYSTEMS ARE AFFECTED?

WHICH AUTHORITIES ARE AFFECTED?

WHICH DELEGATIONS ARE AFFECTED?

WHICH ELIXERS ARE AFFECTED?

WHICH FEDERATIVE RELATIONS ARE AFFECTED?

WHEN DOES THE NEW STATE BEGIN?

WHAT HAPPENS TO EXISTING ACTIONS?

WHAT HAPPENS TO IN-FLIGHT ACTIONS?

Anything not established remains:

UNPROVEN


---

IV. 🧠 BRAINPOWER — MIGRATION ANALYSIS

BRAINPOWER performs the analytical heavy lifting.

It can construct:

Cₙ
 ↓
DIFF
 ↓
DEPENDENCY GRAPH
 ↓
IMPACT ANALYSIS
 ↓
COMPATIBILITY MODEL

It may discover:

DELEGATION X WILL EXPIRE
ELIXER Ω REQUIRES RULE Y
CITADEL B DEPENDS ON POLICY Z
FEDERATION CONTRACT Q IS AFFECTED

But:

BRAINPOWER
≠
MIGRATION AUTHORITY

Its result is:

CANDIDATE MIGRATION ANALYSIS

not authorization.


---

V. 🦆 FOOL — THE MIGRATION CHALLENGE

FOOL attacks the transition itself.

Questions include:

> What breaks when the new Constitution activates?



> Which existing permissions become invalid?



> Which permissions accidentally become broader?



> Does an ELIXER gain authority merely because a rule changed?



> Are any delegations orphaned?



> Does the new Constitution contradict an active federative agreement?



> Can an in-flight action cross the constitutional boundary?



> Can the transition itself be exploited to manufacture authority?



And the ultimate question:

> Can you prove that Cₙ₊₁ actually became the governing state?




---

VI. ⚖️ TRIAS — MIGRATION VALIDATION

TRIAS validates:

SOURCE STATE
      ↓
TARGET STATE
      ↓
MIGRATION AUTHORITY
      ↓
CHANGE SET
      ↓
DEPENDENCY IMPACT
      ↓
COMPATIBILITY
      ↓
TRANSITION CONDITIONS
      ↓
CUTOVER
      ↓
POST-CUTOVER STATE

Possible outcomes:

MIGRATION_APPROVED
MIGRATION_APPROVED_WITH_CONDITIONS
MIGRATION_BLOCKED
MIGRATION_UNPROVEN
MIGRATION_ABORTED

There is no:

PROBABLY_SAFE

as a constitutional state.


---

VII. 🌳 COMPATIBILITY

R6.99 establishes three separate compatibility dimensions.

1. Constitutional Compatibility

Cₙ ↔ Cₙ₊₁

Do the governance states form a valid succession?

2. Operational Compatibility

Cₙ₊₁ ↔ ELIXERS / SYSTEMS

Can existing components operate under the new rules?

3. Federative Compatibility

Cₙ₊₁ ↔ OTHER CITADELS

Does the new state remain compatible with established federative obligations?

These must not be conflated.

CONSTITUTIONAL COMPATIBILITY
≠
OPERATIONAL COMPATIBILITY
≠
FEDERATIVE COMPATIBILITY


---

VIII. 🧬 AUTHORITY MIGRATION

Existing authority must be classified.

For every authority:

AUTHORITY
 ↓
UNCHANGED?
MODIFIED?
RESTRICTED?
EXPIRED?
REVOKED?
REQUIRES REVALIDATION?

The new Constitution must never silently enlarge an existing authority merely because its surrounding rules changed.

Conceptually:

OLD AUTHORITY
      ↓
MIGRATION RULE
      ↓
NEW AUTHORITY STATE

Every transition must be explainable.


---

IX. 🔗 DELEGATION MIGRATION

R6.94–R6.95 now become directly operational.

For each active delegation:

DELEGATION
 ↓
CHECK AGAINST Cₙ₊₁

Possible states:

PRESERVED
NARROWED
EXPIRED
REVOKED
REQUIRES_REVALIDATION
UNPROVEN

A particularly important rule:

> A constitutional migration SHALL NOT silently transform a narrow delegation into a broader delegation.



Thus:

OLD:
DOCUMENT X

cannot become:

NEW:
ALL DOCUMENTS

without explicit constitutional basis.


---

X. 🧪 ELIXER MIGRATION

Every ELIXER operating under the Citadel must have a compatibility relationship with the new Constitution.

Conceptually:

ELIXER Ω
   ↓
REQUIRES
   ↓
CONSTITUTIONAL CAPABILITY SET

Migration evaluates:

SUPPORTED
PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED
INCOMPATIBLE
REQUIRES_UPDATE
QUARANTINED

An incompatible ELIXER must not simply continue operating as though the Constitution had not changed.

Possible response:

Cₙ₊₁
 ↓
ELIXER Ω incompatible
 ↓
QUARANTINE
 ↓
REVALIDATION / UPDATE

This connects directly to the Harbor and Citadel architecture.


---

XI. ⚓ HARBOR — TRANSITION QUARANTINE

R6.99 gives Harbor a specific transition function.

During migration:

NORMAL
  ↓
TRANSITION
  ↓
HIGH-RISK OPERATIONS
  ↓
QUARANTINE / REVIEW

Particularly sensitive actions may require:

PAUSE
VERIFY
REAUTHORIZE

rather than blindly continuing.

The Harbor therefore becomes a constitutional transition buffer.


---

XII. 💧 WATERMARKED CUTOVER

The exact moment of transition becomes a first-class constitutional event:

W₀
MIGRATION PROPOSED

W₁
MIGRATION VALIDATED

W₂
PRE-CUTOVER STATE

W₃
CUTOVER

W₄
Cₙ₊₁ ACTIVE

W₅
POST-CUTOVER VERIFICATION

The critical invariant:

> There SHALL be an identifiable constitutional boundary between Cₙ and Cₙ₊₁.



No ambiguous interval.


---

XIII. ⏳ THE CUTOVER MOMENT

Suppose:

Cₙ
valid until:
12:00:00

Cₙ₊₁
valid from:
12:00:00

Then:

ACTION 11:59:59
→ Cₙ

ACTION 12:00:00
→ Cₙ₊₁

The exact temporal semantics must be deterministic.

No:

11:59-ish

No:

CURRENT VERSION

The Proof Machine must know:

CONSTITUTION(t)


---

XIV. 🚦 IN-FLIGHT ACTIONS

This is one of R6.99's hardest cases.

Suppose:

ACTION START
11:59:59

ACTION COMPLETE
12:00:03

What Constitution applies?

PALACO cannot leave this ambiguous.

The constitutional transition protocol must explicitly define the action's governing temporal model.

For example:

EXECUTION_AUTHORIZATION_TIME

may establish the relevant authority state.

Or the Constitution may explicitly define another deterministic rule.

The key invariant is:

> In-flight behavior SHALL NEVER be resolved by implementation convenience.



The governing rule must be explicit and replayable.


---

XV. 🔄 ABORTED MIGRATION

Suppose:

Cₙ
 ↓
MIGRATION
 ↓
POST-CUTOVER CHECK
 ↓
FAIL

The system must distinguish:

MIGRATION_FAILED

from:

HISTORICAL_ERASURE

The event remains.

Cₙ
 ↓
ATTEMPTED Cₙ₊₁
 ↓
FAILURE
 ↓
Cₙ REMAINS GOVERNING

unless the transition had already validly completed.

Thus:

> A failed migration is itself historical state.




---

XVI. 🚨 ROLLBACK ≠ TIME TRAVEL

If Cₙ₊₁ fails operationally and the system returns to Cₙ:

Cₙ
 ↓
Cₙ₊₁
 ↓
ROLLBACK
 ↓
Cₙ

this must not be represented as though Cₙ₊₁ never existed.

Correct:

Cₙ
 ↓
Cₙ₊₁
 ↓
ROLLBACK EVENT
 ↓
Cₙ₊₂

where Cₙ₊₂ may explicitly restore prior governance semantics.

This is crucial.

> Rollback restores a governance configuration; it does not reverse history.




---

XVII. ⚓ QUAY — MIGRATION MEMORY

Quay receives:

MIGRATION_PROPOSED
MIGRATION_ANALYZED
MIGRATION_VALIDATED
MIGRATION_BLOCKED
MIGRATION_STARTED
MIGRATION_CUTOVER
MIGRATION_VERIFIED
MIGRATION_FAILED
MIGRATION_ABORTED
MIGRATION_ROLLED_BACK

Therefore:

STATE HISTORY

becomes:

Cₙ
 ↓
MIGRATION
 ↓
Cₙ₊₁
 ↓
MIGRATION RESULT

Everything remains replayable.


