XXV. 🌱 THE R6.99 PRINCIPLE

> Constitutional evolution is not an overwrite. It is a provable transition between immutable governance states.



And:

> A safe transition does not merely establish where governance ends up; it proves how it got there.



And:

> Rollback may restore a state of operation, but it never restores the past.



This creates the missing bridge between:

constitutional evolution

and

operational continuity.


