UNPROVEN


---

XIII. 🚨 CONSTITUTIONAL CONFLICT

Suppose:

A:
ALLOW X

B:
DENY X

The Federation cannot simply say:

MAJORITY WINS

That would confuse consensus with truth.

Instead:

A → ALLOW
B → DENY
      ↓
CONFLICT
      ↓
FEDERATION RULE
      ↓
TRIAS

Possible result:

BLOCKED

unless a valid federative rule explicitly establishes another outcome.

This preserves the fundamental PALACO principle:

> The Federation does not vote reality into existence.




