☄️🌱 R7.01 — HORTUS FEDERATION MEMBERSHIP, ADMISSION, SUSPENSION, EXIT & SUCCESSION PROTOCOL

Status: CANONICAL ENGINEERING BUILD

R7.00 proved that independently governed Citadels can interoperate across constitutional versions.

R7.01 now establishes the missing premise:

> A federation cannot safely coordinate constitutional systems unless federation membership itself is a governed, evidenced, bounded, versioned, and replayable state.



The federation becomes an organism.

But never a super-Citadel.


---

I. 👑 THE R7.01 PROBLEM

R7.00 assumed:

FEDERATION
    │
    ├── CITADEL A
    ├── CITADEL B
    └── CITADEL C

R7.01 asks:

WHO MAY ENTER?

WHO MAY PARTICIPATE?

WHO MAY BE SUSPENDED?

WHO MAY LEAVE?

WHO MAY REPRESENT A DEPARTED MEMBER?

WHAT HAPPENS WHEN A CITADEL SPLITS?

WHAT HAPPENS WHEN TWO CITADELS MERGE?

WHAT HAPPENS WHEN THE FEDERATION CHANGES VERSION?

WHAT HAPPENS WHEN MEMBERS DISAGREE WITH THAT CHANGE?

These are not administrative questions.

They alter the constitutional state against which future federated actions are evaluated.

Therefore:

MEMBERSHIP = CONSTITUTIONAL STATE


---

II. 🌐 FEDERATION IS NOT A SUPER-CITADEL

R7.01 establishes the first boundary:

FEDERATION
    ≠
SUPER-CITADEL

The federation may possess:

membership rules
participation rules
federative agreements
shared scopes
protocol versions
admission criteria
suspension mechanisms
exit mechanisms
succession rules
conflict procedures

But it does not automatically possess:

local constitutional sovereignty
over member Citadels

Thus:

FEDERATION
     │
     ├── governs FEDERATION STATE
     │
     └── does not govern LOCAL CONSTITUTIONAL STATE

This distinction is foundational.


---

III. 🌱 Z.A.N.D. — NO IMPLIED MEMBERSHIP

R7.00 established:

NO IMPLIED COMPATIBILITY

R7.01 extends this:

NO IMPLIED MEMBERSHIP

Therefore:

CITADEL EXISTS
       ↓
DOES NOT IMPLY
       ↓
FEDERATION MEMBER

Likewise:

PAST MEMBER
       ↓
DOES NOT IMPLY
       ↓
CURRENT MEMBER

And:

MEMBER
       ↓
DOES NOT IMPLY
       ↓
UNLIMITED PARTICIPATION

Membership must be:

IDENTIFIED
+
CONSENTED
+
AUTHORIZED
+
EVIDENCED
+
BOUNDED
+
TEMPORALLY VALID


---

IV. 🧬 THE FEDERATION MEMBERSHIP RECORD

R7.01 introduces:

FederationMembership

Conceptually:

FederationMembership {
    membership_id
    federation_id
    citadel_id
    constitutional_identity
    constitutional_version
    admission_authority
    admission_consent
    participation_scope
    effective_from
    effective_until
    status
    applicable_federation_version
    delegation_state
    suspension_state
    exit_state
    succession_state
    provenance
    evidence
    watermark
}

The membership record is therefore not merely:

member = true

It is a historical constitutional fact with provenance.


---

V. 🚪 ADMISSION

Admission becomes an explicit protocol.

APPLICATION
    ↓
Z.A.N.D.
    ↓
IDENTITY VERIFICATION
    ↓
CONSTITUTIONAL STATE IDENTIFICATION
    ↓
VERSION IDENTIFICATION
    ↓
CAPABILITY DISCLOSURE
    ↓
AUTHORITY VERIFICATION
    ↓
CONSENT VERIFICATION
    ↓
COMPATIBILITY ANALYSIS
    ↓
FOOL CHALLENGE
    ↓
TRIAS DETERMINATION
    ↓
WATERMARK
    ↓
MEMBERSHIP ACTIVATION
    ↓
QUAY

No shortcut:

INVITATION
   ↓
MEMBER

An invitation is not membership.


---

VI. ⚖️ ADMISSION DOES NOT TRANSFER SOVEREIGNTY

A Citadel entering a federation does not surrender its constitutional identity.

Instead:

CITADEL C₇
     │
     ├── remains C₇
     │
     └── becomes member of Fₙ

Therefore:

MEMBERSHIP
=
ADDITIONAL FEDERATIVE RELATION

not:

MEMBERSHIP
=
CONSTITUTIONAL REPLACEMENT


---

VII. 🛂 PARTICIPATION SCOPE

Membership and participation are separate.

A Citadel may be:

MEMBER

while being authorized only for:

READ
+
VERIFY

and not:

EXECUTE
+
EXPORT
+
DELEGATE

Therefore:

MEMBERSHIP
∩
PARTICIPATION_SCOPE

determines actual federative participation.

This preserves R7.00's narrowest-boundary principle.


---

VIII. 🟢 ACTIVE MEMBERSHIP

A member is active only when:

IDENTITY
+
MEMBERSHIP
+
AUTHORITY
+
SCOPE
+
TIME
+
FEDERATION_VERSION

are all valid.

Thus:

ACTIVE
≠
HISTORICALLY_ADMITTED

A membership may exist historically while being inactive now.


---

IX. ⏸️ SUSPENSION

Suspension becomes a first-class state:

ACTIVE
  ↓
SUSPENDED

Suspension does not necessarily mean:

MEMBERSHIP DESTROYED

Instead:

MEMBERSHIP EXISTS
        │
        └── PARTICIPATION TEMPORARILY DISABLED

A suspended member therefore cannot silently continue participating under its former active authority.


---

X. 🚨 SUSPENSION TRIGGERS

Potential triggers include:

CONSTITUTIONAL INVALIDITY
SECURITY BREACH
EVIDENCE FAILURE
WATERMARK FAILURE
VERSION INCOMPATIBILITY
UNRESOLVED CONFLICT
AUTHORITY EXPIRATION
REVOCATION
PROTOCOL NON-COMPLIANCE
FEDERATIVE EMERGENCY

But:

> Suspension itself must be authorized and evidenced.



The federation cannot simply declare:

SUSPEND A

without a constitutional basis.


---

XI. 🔓 EXIT

A member may leave voluntarily where permitted.

Canonical transition:

ACTIVE
   ↓
EXIT REQUEST
   ↓
AUTHORITY CHECK
   ↓
OBLIGATION CHECK
   ↓
DEPENDENCY CHECK
   ↓
TRIAS
   ↓
EXIT DETERMINATION
   ↓
WATERMARK
   ↓
MEMBERSHIP ENDS

Critically:

EXIT
≠
ERASURE

Historical membership remains in Quay.


---

XII. ⚓ POST-EXIT PROVENANCE

Suppose:

A

was a member from:

10:00 → 14:00

and exited at:

14:00

A replay at:

12:00

must still reconstruct:

A = MEMBER

A replay at:

15:00

must reconstruct:

A = FORMER_MEMBER

Therefore:

MEMBERSHIP(t)

becomes part of FEDERATED_STATE(t).


---

XIII. 🧬 SUCCESSION

The most difficult case is succession.

Suppose:

CITADEL A

is replaced by:

CITADEL A'

The federation cannot assume:

A' = A

Succession must be proven.

Potential succession evidence:

SUCCESSION CLAIM
+
ORIGINATING AUTHORITY
+
IDENTITY CONTINUITY
+
CONSTITUTIONAL CONTINUITY
+
ASSET / STATE CONTINUITY
+
DELEGATION CONTINUITY
+
FEDERATIVE ACCEPTANCE

Only then may:

A'

inherit defined federative obligations or privileges.


---

XIV. 🚫 NO AUTOMATIC SUCCESSION

R7.01 establishes:

> Organizational continuity SHALL NOT automatically imply constitutional continuity.



Therefore:

A → A'

does not automatically mean:

AUTHORITY(A)
   ↓
AUTHORITY(A')

Nor:

MEMBERSHIP(A)
   ↓
MEMBERSHIP(A')

Every inherited property must have a provenance path.


---

XV. 🧩 SPLIT

Suppose:

CITADEL A

splits into:

A₁
A₂

The federation must not automatically produce:

A₁ = MEMBER
A₂ = MEMBER

Instead:

A
 ↓
SPLIT EVENT
 ↓
A₁
A₂
 ↓
SUCCESSION ANALYSIS
 ↓
TRIAS

Each resulting Citadel receives only the authority and federative status that can be independently proven.

This prevents authority multiplication through organizational division.


---

XVI. 🔗 MERGE

Likewise:

A + B
   ↓
C

does not automatically mean:

AUTHORITY(A) + AUTHORITY(B)
          ↓
     AUTHORITY(C)

That would create precisely the authority amplification R7.00 prohibits.

Instead:

A AUTHORITY
B AUTHORITY
     ↓
MERGER ANALYSIS
     ↓
C CONSTITUTIONAL STATE
     ↓
TRIAS
     ↓
NEW FEDERATIVE STATUS


---

XVII. ☄️ THE NO-AMALGAMATION RULE

R7.01 therefore extends:

FEDERATED_CAPABILITY
≤
PROVEN_INTERSECTION

with:

SUCCESSION_CAPABILITY
≤
PROVEN_INHERITED_AUTHORITY

and:

MERGED_CAPABILITY
≤
PROVEN_NEW_CONSTITUTIONAL_AUTHORITY

No organizational event may manufacture authority.


---

XVIII. 📜 FEDERATION PROTOCOL VERSIONING

The federation itself evolves.

Therefore:

FEDERATION F₃
      ↓
FEDERATION F₄

is not merely a software update.

It is a federative constitutional transition.

Members must therefore know:

WHICH FEDERATION VERSION
WAS ACTIVE?

at every relevant moment.


---

XIX. ⏳ FEDERATION STATE OVER TIME

R7.01 introduces:

FEDERATION_STATE(t)

which contains at least:

FEDERATION_VERSION(t)
MEMBERS(t)
SUSPENSIONS(t)
EXITS(t)
SUCCESSIONS(t)
PARTICIPATION_SCOPES(t)
ACTIVE_CONTRACTS(t)
FEDERATION_RULES(t)

Therefore:

FEDERATED_STATE(t)
=
FEDERATION_STATE(t)
+
LOCAL_STATES(t)
+
INTEROPERABILITY_STATE(t)

This is the historical substrate for R5.


---

XX. 🦆 FOOL — MEMBERSHIP CHALLENGE

FOOL receives a new responsibility.

It must be able to challenge:

WHO ADMITTED THIS MEMBER?

WAS CONSENT VALID?

WAS THE MEMBER'S CONSTITUTION CORRECTLY IDENTIFIED?

WAS THE FEDERATION VERSION CORRECT?

WAS THE MEMBER ACTUALLY ACTIVE?

WAS SUSPENSION VALID?

WAS EXIT VALID?

IS SUCCESSION PROVEN?

DID A SPLIT MULTIPLY AUTHORITY?

DID A MERGER AMALGAMATE AUTHORITY?

IS THE CURRENT MEMBER REALLY THE HISTORICAL MEMBER?

FOOL does not determine the answer.

It prevents unchallenged assumptions.


---

XXI. 🧠 BRAINPOWER — FEDERATION ANALYSIS

BRAINPOWER receives:

FEDERATION_STATE
+
MEMBERSHIP_RECORDS
+
CONSTITUTIONAL_STATES
+
SUCCESSION_EVENTS
+
FEDERATIVE_CONTRACTS

and generates:

CANDIDATE FEDERATION STATE

But:

BRAINPOWER
≠
FEDERATION AUTHORITY

The chain remains:

BRAINPOWER
    ↓
ANALYSIS
    ↓
EVIDENCE
    ↓
FOOL
    ↓
TRIAS
    ↓
DETERMINATION


---

XXII. ⚖️ TRIAS — FEDERATION STATE DETERMINATION

TRIAS determines:

MEMBER
NON_MEMBER
SUSPENDED
EXITED
SUCCESSOR
NON_SUCCESSOR
COMPATIBLE
INCOMPATIBLE
VALID_TRANSITION
INVALID_TRANSITION
UNPROVEN

The federation does not get to override the determination merely because doing so would be convenient.


---

XXIII. 💧 WATERMARK — MEMBERSHIP LINEAGE

Every material membership transition receives a watermark.

Example:

W_F
    FEDERATION ID

W_M
    MEMBERSHIP ID

W_C
    CONSTITUTIONAL STATE

W_A
    ADMISSION AUTHORITY

W_S
    SCOPE

W_T
    TIME

W_E
    EVIDENCE

W_TR
    TRIAS DETERMINATION

Thus:

MEMBERSHIP
=
WATERMARKED CONSTITUTIONAL EVENT


---

XXIV. ⚓ QUAY — THE FEDERATION LEDGER

Quay must preserve transitions, not merely current status.

Example:

A
↓
APPLIED
↓
ADMITTED
↓
ACTIVE
↓
SUSPENDED
↓
REACTIVATED
↓
EXITED

The final state:

EXITED

is insufficient by itself.

Quay must retain the causal chain explaining:

WHY
WHO
WHEN
UNDER WHICH FEDERATION VERSION
UNDER WHICH AUTHORITY
WITH WHICH CONSENT
WITH WHICH SCOPE
WITH WHICH EVIDENCE


---

XXV. 🧪 R5 — FEDERATION REPLAY

A historical verifier must be able to execute:

REPLAY FEDERATION AT T

and reconstruct:

FEDERATION_VERSION(t)
        ↓
MEMBERS(t)
        ↓
MEMBERSHIP_SCOPE(t)
        ↓
SUSPENSIONS(t)
        ↓
EXIT(t)
        ↓
SUCCESSION(t)
        ↓
CONTRACTS(t)
        ↓
CONSTITUTIONAL_STATES(t)
        ↓
INTEROPERABILITY(t)
        ↓
AUTHORITY(t)

Possible outcomes:

MEMBER
NON_MEMBER
SUSPENDED
EXITED
SUCCESSOR_VALID
SUCCESSOR_UNPROVEN
INVALID_TRANSITION
CONFLICTED
EXPIRED
REVOKED
UNPROVEN


---

XXVI. 🌸 HARUM — HUMAN FEDERATION STATE

The user should never need to understand the internal graph.

Instead:

> Your Citadel is currently an active member of the federation.



> Your participation is limited to verification and analysis.



> A protocol transition is scheduled.



> Your Citadel has not yet consented to the new federation protocol.



> Participation is suspended pending verification.



> This Citadel's claimed succession has not been proven.



HARUM explains the state.

It does not create it.


---

XXVII. 🔥 FEDERATION PROTOCOL TRANSITION

The most important new state transition becomes:

F₃
 ↓
MIGRATION
 ↓
F₄

But membership must be evaluated again.

A member may:

ACCEPT F₄

while another may:

REJECT F₄

The federation therefore cannot silently assume:

F₃ MEMBERS
=
F₄ MEMBERS

The transition must establish:

WHO REMAINS
WHO EXITS
WHO SUSPENDS
WHO RE-QUALIFIES


---

XXVIII. 🚨 FEDERATION SPLIT

The ultimate stress case:

FEDERATION F
       │
       ├──────── F₁
       │
       └──────── F₂

R7.01 refuses:

F₁ + F₂
=
same federation

without proof.

Each resulting federation must establish:

IDENTITY
MEMBERSHIP
PROTOCOL
AUTHORITY
CONTRACTS
SUCCESSION
PROVENANCE

independently.


---

XXIX. 🌳 HORTUS FEDERATION LIFE CYCLE

The federation now possesses an explicit lifecycle:

┌───────────────┐
                    │   PROPOSED    │
                    └───────┬───────┘
                            ↓
                       ADMISSION
                            ↓
                         ACTIVE
                       ↙        ↘
                 SUSPENSION     EXIT
                    ↓             ↓
                REACTIVATE      EXITED
                    │
                    └──────→ ACTIVE

                    ACTIVE
                       ↓
                   SUCCESSION
                       ↓
                 NEW MEMBER STATE

                    ACTIVE
                       ↓
                     SPLIT
                    ↙     ↘
                  A₁       A₂

                    ACTIVE
                       ↓
                    MERGE
                       ↓
                      C

Every arrow is:

EXPLICIT
AUTHORIZED
EVIDENCED
WATERMARKED
REPLAYABLE


---

XXX. 🔱 R7.01 CANONICAL INVARIANTS

FED-M01

Federation membership SHALL NOT confer constitutional sovereignty over a member.

FED-M02

Membership SHALL be explicit and evidenced.

FED-M03

Membership SHALL be temporally bounded where applicable.

FED-M04

Admission SHALL require verifiable authority and consent.

FED-M05

Membership SHALL possess explicit participation scope.

FED-M06

Suspension SHALL be an explicit constitutional state transition.

FED-M07

Exit SHALL NOT erase historical membership provenance.

FED-M08

Federation membership SHALL NOT be implied by participation or invitation.

FED-M09

Succession SHALL require explicit proof of applicable continuity.

FED-M10

Succession SHALL NOT automatically transfer constitutional authority.

FED-M11

A Citadel split SHALL NOT automatically multiply federative authority.

FED-M12

A Citadel merger SHALL NOT automatically amalgamate constitutional authority.

FED-M13

Federation protocol changes SHALL be versioned.

FED-M14

Membership SHALL be evaluated against the applicable federation version.

FED-M15

Federation state SHALL be historically reconstructible.

FED-M16

BRAINPOWER SHALL NOT independently establish membership.

FED-M17

FOOL SHALL be able to challenge membership and succession claims.

FED-M18

TRIAS SHALL determine disputed federative state transitions.

FED-M19

Material membership transitions SHALL be watermarked.

FED-M20

Quay SHALL preserve the complete membership lifecycle.

FED-M21

Federation state SHALL be replayable.

FED-M22

A federation split SHALL produce independently verifiable federative identities.

FED-M23

A federation merge SHALL require explicit constitutional determination.

FED-M24

No federation lifecycle transition SHALL silently amplify authority.

FED-M25

A verifier SHALL be able to reconstruct why a Citadel was, or was not, a valid federation member at time t.


---

