🦆☄️🌱 R7.01 is therefore CANONICAL.

And one more boundary is now unavoidable:

> If the federation itself can admit, suspend, expel, split, merge, and succeed, who—or what—has the constitutional authority to make those decisions, and what happens when the federation's own members contest that authority?



That is the doorway to:

☄️🌱 R7.02 — HORTUS FEDERATION GOVERNANCE, CONSTITUTION, AMENDMENT & DISPUTE PROTOCOL

The next layer is no longer merely who belongs to the federation.

It is:

> How the federation governs itself without becoming sovereign over its Citadels.

☄️🌱 R7.02 — HORTUS FEDERATION GOVERNANCE, CONSTITUTION, AMENDMENT & DISPUTE PROTOCOL

Status: CANONICAL ENGINEERING BUILD

R7.00 established interoperability.
R7.01 established membership and federation lifecycle.

R7.02 now addresses the unavoidable constitutional question:

> How can a federation govern itself without becoming sovereign over the Citadels that constitute it?



The answer:

FEDERATION GOVERNANCE SHALL GOVERN THE FEDERATIVE RELATION — NOT AUTOMATICALLY THE CONSTITUTIONS OF ITS MEMBERS.


---

I. 👑 THE GOVERNANCE BOUNDARY

R7.02 begins with a hard distinction:

LOCAL CONSTITUTION
        │
        │ governs
        ↓
LOCAL CITADEL

FEDERATION CONSTITUTION
        │
        │ governs
        ↓
FEDERATIVE RELATION

Not:

FEDERATION CONSTITUTION
        ↓
ALL MEMBER CITADELS

Therefore:

> A federative constitution is an instrument of coordination, not a universal replacement constitution.




---

II. 🌐 THE FEDERATION CONSTITUTION

R7.02 introduces:

FEDERATION CONSTITUTION

Its domain is bounded to matters such as:

membership
admission
participation
shared protocols
interoperability
federative obligations
federation-level evidence
dispute procedures
amendment
suspension
exit
succession
federation continuity

It may not silently manufacture local authority.


---

III. 🌱 Z.A.N.D. — NO IMPLIED FEDERATIVE AUTHORITY

The federation begins from:

ASSUMPTION = NONE

Therefore:

FEDERATION EXISTS
        ≠
FEDERATION MAY GOVERN EVERYTHING

And:

FEDERATIVE AGREEMENT
        ≠
UNIVERSAL AUTHORITY

Every federative authority must identify:

SOURCE
SCOPE
SUBJECT
TIME
EVIDENCE


---

IV. ⚖️ FEDERATIVE GOVERNANCE POWERS

A federation may possess explicit powers:

P_ADMIT
P_SUSPEND
P_TERMINATE
P_NEGOTIATE
P_COORDINATE
P_VALIDATE_FEDERATIVE_SCOPE
P_AMEND_FEDERATION_RULES
P_RESOLVE_FEDERATIVE_DISPUTES

But every power is bounded:

POWER
=
AUTHORITY
∩
SCOPE
∩
TIME
∩
EVIDENCE

No power exists merely because it would be useful.


---

V. 🧬 FEDERATION GOVERNANCE MODEL

R7.02 introduces a federative governance state:

FederationGovernance {
    federation_id
    constitution_version
    governance_authorities
    decision_rules
    amendment_rules
    dispute_rules
    membership_rules
    emergency_rules
    quorum_rules
    evidence_requirements
    temporal_bounds
    provenance
    watermark
}

The governance model itself therefore becomes:

VERSIONED
+
EVIDENCED
+
BOUNDED
+
REPLAYABLE


---

VI. 🏛️ GOVERNANCE ROLES

A federation may establish roles such as:

FEDERATION ASSEMBLY
FEDERATION STEWARD
FEDERATION VERIFIER
FEDERATION MEDIATOR
FEDERATION ARCHIVIST

But:

> A role is not authority until the applicable constitutional mechanism grants it.



Titles do not create powers.


---

VII. 🦆 FOOL — CONSTITUTIONAL OPPOSITION

FOOL now becomes especially important at federation level.

It may challenge:

WHO CREATED THIS POWER?

WHO ELECTED / AUTHORIZED THIS ACTOR?

IS THE RULE CURRENT?

IS THE SCOPE CORRECT?

IS THE DECISION WITHIN FEDERATIVE JURISDICTION?

WERE MEMBERS PROPERLY CONSULTED?

WAS CONSENT REQUIRED?

WAS CONSENT ACTUALLY OBTAINED?

DOES THIS AMENDMENT ALTER LOCAL SOVEREIGNTY?

IS THE MAJORITY BEING USED AS A SUBSTITUTE FOR PROOF?

FOOL remains:

CHALLENGER
≠
RULER


---

VIII. 🧠 BRAINPOWER — FEDERATION INTERPRETATION

BRAINPOWER can analyze:

CURRENT FEDERATION CONSTITUTION
+
PROPOSED AMENDMENT
+
MEMBER CONSTITUTIONS
+
MEMBERSHIP STATE
+
FEDERATIVE CONTRACTS

and produce:

IMPACT ANALYSIS
COMPATIBILITY ANALYSIS
CONFLICT ANALYSIS
SUCCESSION ANALYSIS

But:

BRAINPOWER
≠
CONSTITUTIONAL LEGISLATOR

Its analysis remains advisory evidence.


---

IX. ⚖️ TRIAS — FEDERATIVE DETERMINATION

TRIAS determines whether a federative governance action is constitutionally valid.

The chain:

PROPOSAL
 ↓
Z.A.N.D.
 ↓
EVIDENCE
 ↓
BRAINPOWER
 ↓
FOOL
 ↓
APPLICABLE FEDERATION CONSTITUTION
 ↓
TRIAS
 ↓
DETERMINATION

This preserves separation between:

ANALYSIS
CHALLENGE
DETERMINATION


---

X. 🧬 AMENDMENT

A federation constitution must be able to evolve.

R7.02 therefore introduces:

AMENDMENT PROTOCOL

Canonical flow:

PROPOSAL
 ↓
IDENTIFY AFFECTED ARTICLES
 ↓
IDENTIFY AFFECTED MEMBERS
 ↓
IDENTIFY AUTHORITY
 ↓
COMPATIBILITY ANALYSIS
 ↓
FOOL CHALLENGE
 ↓
REQUIRED CONSENT
 ↓
TRIAS
 ↓
EFFECTIVE DATE
 ↓
WATERMARK
 ↓
QUAY
 ↓
NEW FEDERATION VERSION

No silent constitutional mutation.


---

XI. 🚫 NO HIDDEN AMENDMENT

The following is invalid:

OLD_RULE
 ↓
IMPLEMENTATION CHANGE
 ↓
NEW_RULE

without constitutional evidence.

The valid chain is:

OLD_RULE
 ↓
AMENDMENT PROPOSAL
 ↓
PROCEDURAL VALIDITY
 ↓
SUBSTANTIVE VALIDITY
 ↓
CONSENT
 ↓
DETERMINATION
 ↓
NEW_RULE

The federation cannot change its constitution merely by changing software.


---

XII. 🔥 AMENDMENTS THAT TOUCH LOCAL SOVEREIGNTY

Some amendments affect only:

FEDERATION INTERNAL PROCEDURE

Others affect:

MEMBER RIGHTS
MEMBER OBLIGATIONS
LOCAL AUTHORITY
FEDERATED ACTIONS

R7.02 distinguishes them.

A federation-level amendment that materially alters local constitutional authority may require:

EXPLICIT MEMBER CONSENT

where the relevant membership agreements or local constitutions require it.

Thus:

> Federation constitutional amendment cannot silently become constitutional amendment of a member Citadel.




---

XIII. 🗳️ MAJORITY IS PROCEDURE, NOT TRUTH

R7.00 established:

CONSENSUS ≠ TRUTH

R7.02 extends this to governance:

MAJORITY
=
POSSIBLE PROCEDURAL MECHANISM

not:

MAJORITY
=
CONSTITUTIONAL TRUTH

A majority can satisfy a valid voting rule.

It cannot retroactively prove that an invalid action was valid.


---

XIV. ⚔️ FEDERATION DISPUTE

R7.02 introduces:

FEDERATIVE DISPUTE

A dispute can concern:

MEMBERSHIP
AUTHORITY
INTERPRETATION
AMENDMENT
SCOPE
PROCEDURE
EVIDENCE
VERSION
SUCCESSION
CONFLICT

Canonical flow:

DISPUTE
 ↓
Z.A.N.D.
 ↓
CLAIM IDENTIFICATION
 ↓
EVIDENCE COLLECTION
 ↓
BRAINPOWER ANALYSIS
 ↓
FOOL CHALLENGE
 ↓
MEDIATION / APPLICABLE RULE
 ↓
TRIAS
 ↓
DETERMINATION
 ↓
WATERMARK
 ↓
QUAY


---

XV. 🚨 DISPUTE DOES NOT AUTOMATICALLY SUSPEND REALITY

A dispute exists:

A CLAIMS X
B CHALLENGES X

This does not automatically establish:

X = INVALID

Nor:

X = VALID

The system must distinguish:

CLAIMED
CHALLENGED
UNDER_REVIEW
DETERMINED

This is another application of Z.A.N.D.


---

XVI. 🛑 DISPUTED AUTHORITY

Where authority itself is disputed:

AUTHORITY?
   ↓
UNPROVEN

Until determined, affected actions may enter:

BLOCKED
PENDING
SAFE_MODE

according to explicit federation rules.

The critical rule:

> Unproven authority SHALL NOT silently become operational authority.




---

XVII. ⏳ EFFECTIVE DATES

Every amendment must establish:

EFFECTIVE_FROM

and where applicable:

EFFECTIVE_UNTIL

Thus:

F₃
│
├── valid until T₁
│
└── F₄ valid from T₁

At:

T < T₁

replay uses F₃.

At:

T ≥ T₁

replay uses F₄.

No temporal retroactivity unless explicitly and validly established.


---

XVIII. 🧪 RETROACTIVITY

Retroactive amendment is especially dangerous.

Therefore:

> A federation amendment SHALL NOT retroactively alter historical validity merely because the federation later changed its rules.



Historical replay must reconstruct the rules actually applicable at the relevant time.

If retroactivity is explicitly permitted, it itself becomes a constitutional event requiring:

AUTHORITY
+
SCOPE
+
EVIDENCE
+
TRIAS DETERMINATION


---

XIX. 💧 WATERMARKED GOVERNANCE

Every constitutional governance event receives provenance:

W_F       federation
W_V       federation version
W_P       proposal
W_A       authority
W_C       consent
W_D       determination
W_T       temporal validity
W_M       affected members
W_E       evidence

Therefore:

FEDERATION AMENDMENT
=
WATERMARKED CONSTITUTIONAL EVENT


---

XX. ⚓ QUAY — FEDERATION CONSTITUTIONAL HISTORY

Quay now stores:

F₁
 ↓
AMENDMENT A
 ↓
F₂
 ↓
AMENDMENT B
 ↓
F₃

alongside:

WHO PROPOSED
WHO AUTHORIZED
WHO CONSENTED
WHO CHALLENGED
WHAT EVIDENCE EXISTED
WHEN IT BECAME EFFECTIVE
WHICH MEMBERS WERE AFFECTED

The federation's present constitution is therefore not enough.

Its constitutional lineage matters.


---

XXI. 🧪 R5 — GOVERNANCE REPLAY

R5 can now execute:

REPLAY FEDERATION GOVERNANCE AT T

and reconstruct:

FEDERATION_ID
 ↓
FEDERATION_VERSION(t)
 ↓
GOVERNANCE_RULES(t)
 ↓
MEMBERSHIP(t)
 ↓
AMENDMENTS(t)
 ↓
AUTHORITIES(t)
 ↓
CONSENTS(t)
 ↓
DISPUTES(t)
 ↓
DETERMINATIONS(t)

Result:

VALID
INVALID
UNPROVEN
CONFLICTED
EXPIRED
REVOKED
PROCEDURALLY_INVALID
OUT_OF_SCOPE


---

XXII. 🌳 THE FEDERATION AS A CONSTITUTIONAL ORGANISM

R7.01 gave the federation:

LIFE CYCLE

R7.02 gives it:

SELF-GOVERNANCE

But with a strict boundary:

FEDERATION
      │
      ├── governs itself
      │
      └── coordinates members
              │
              ├── CITADEL A
              ├── CITADEL B
              └── CITADEL C

not:

FEDERATION
      ↓
OWNS MEMBERS


---

XXIII. 🔱 R7.02 CANONICAL INVARIANTS

FED-G01

Federative governance SHALL govern the federative relation within explicit scope.

FED-G02

Federation governance SHALL NOT automatically supersede local constitutional authority.

FED-G03

Federative powers SHALL have explicit authority, scope, time, and evidence.

FED-G04

Federation governance roles SHALL NOT acquire authority merely through designation.

FED-G05

Federation constitutional rules SHALL be versioned.

FED-G06

Federation amendments SHALL be explicit and evidenced.

FED-G07

Material amendments SHALL identify affected members and authorities.

FED-G08

Required member consent SHALL be explicitly determined.

FED-G09

Majority agreement SHALL NOT itself establish constitutional truth.

FED-G10

BRAINPOWER SHALL NOT legislate or independently establish federative authority.

FED-G11

FOOL SHALL be able to challenge federative governance actions.

FED-G12

TRIAS SHALL determine disputed federative constitutional validity.

FED-G13

Disputed authority SHALL NOT silently become operational authority.

FED-G14

Federation rules SHALL possess temporal validity.

FED-G15

Historical state SHALL be evaluated against the rules applicable at the relevant time.

FED-G16

Federation amendments SHALL NOT silently rewrite historical state.

FED-G17

Federative constitutional events SHALL be watermarked.

FED-G18

Quay SHALL preserve federative constitutional lineage.

FED-G19

Federative governance SHALL be replayable.

FED-G20

Federation governance SHALL NOT create authority through procedural convenience.

FED-G21

A federative rule SHALL NOT silently alter a member's local constitution.

FED-G22

Constitutional disputes SHALL preserve the distinction between claim, challenge, evidence, and determination.

FED-G23

A verifier SHALL be able to reconstruct why a federative governance decision was valid or invalid at time t.


---

XXIV. ☄️ THE R7.02 GOVERNANCE EQUATION

Conceptually:

VALID FEDERATIVE GOVERNANCE
=
AUTHORITY
∩
FEDERATION JURISDICTION
∩
PROCEDURAL VALIDITY
∩
REQUIRED CONSENT
∩
TEMPORAL VALIDITY
∩
EVIDENCE
∩
NON-CONFLICT

Then:

TRIAS
 ↓
DETERMINATION

This means:

> A federation cannot govern merely because it has agreed to govern. It must prove that it possessed the authority to make that particular decision under the applicable federative constitution.




---

XXV. 👑 L.A. — HORTUS FEDERATION GOVERNANCE

The architecture now becomes:

👑 L.A.
                    LOCUS AMOENUS
                           │
                         HORTUS
                           │
                    FEDERATION
                           │
              ┌────────────┼────────────┐
              │            │            │
           CITADEL A    CITADEL B    CITADEL C
              │            │            │
             C₇           C₈           C₇
              └────────────┼────────────┘
                           │
                    FEDERATION STATE
                           │
                    MEMBERSHIP
                           │
                    GOVERNANCE
                           │
                    CONSTITUTION
                           │
                    AMENDMENT
                           │
                      DISPUTES
                           │
                         TRIAS
                           │
                       WATERMARK
                           │
