XXVI. 🔱 R7.03 CANONICAL INVARIANTS

FED-C01

Constitutional conflict SHALL be represented explicitly.

FED-C02

Conflict SHALL NOT automatically be treated as system failure.

FED-C03

Federative adjudication SHALL require demonstrable jurisdiction.

FED-C04

No actor SHALL acquire adjudicative authority merely by asserting it.

FED-C05

BRAINPOWER SHALL analyze conflict but SHALL NOT independently adjudicate.

FED-C06

FOOL SHALL be able to challenge claims, jurisdiction, evidence, and remedies.

FED-C07

TRIAS SHALL determine federative constitutional validity within its authorized scope.

FED-C08

Deadlock SHALL be represented as a distinct constitutional state.

FED-C09

Deadlock SHALL NOT itself create override authority.

FED-C10

Unresolved authority SHALL NOT silently become operational authority.

FED-C11

Provisional determinations SHALL be explicitly marked and temporally bounded.

FED-C12

Remedies SHALL NOT exceed the authority of the adjudicating mechanism.

FED-C13

Corrective actions SHALL themselves be authorized and evidenced.

FED-C14

Conflict state SHALL be historically reconstructible.

FED-C15

Conflict events SHALL be watermarked.

FED-C16

Quay SHALL preserve complete conflict lineage.

FED-C17

R5 SHALL replay federative conflicts against the applicable historical state.

FED-C18

Procedural finality SHALL NOT be represented as metaphysical truth.

FED-C19

New evidence or a changed constitutional state SHALL be capable of creating a new claim where permitted.

FED-C20

Federative conflict resolution SHALL NOT silently modify local constitutional sovereignty.

FED-C21

Majority preference SHALL NOT replace constitutional proof.

FED-C22

A verifier SHALL be able to reconstruct why a conflict was resolved, blocked, or left unproven.


