 ↓
COMPATIBILITY
 ↓
MEMBER CONSEQUENCES
 ↓
CONSENT
 ↓
FOOL
 ↓
TRIAS
 ↓
MIGRATION
 ↓
F₄

The old constitution does not disappear.

It becomes part of constitutional history.


---

II. 🌱 Z.A.N.D. — OLD ≠ INVALID

A crucial distinction:

F₃

becoming superseded by:

F₄

does not mean:

F₃ = FALSE

Nor:

F₃ = NEVER VALID

Instead:

F₃
=
VALID HISTORICAL CONSTITUTIONAL STATE

for its applicable temporal domain.

Therefore:

SUPERSEDED ≠ INVALIDATED

This is essential for R5 replay.


---

