IV. 🔱 CONSTITUTIONAL IDENTITY

A federation needs continuity.

Therefore:

F₃ → F₄

requires an explicit determination of whether:

FEDERATION_IDENTITY_CONTINUES

or:

FEDERATION_TERMINATES
+
NEW_FEDERATION_CREATED

These are not equivalent.


---

V. 🚫 NO IDENTITY BY DECLARATION

A document saying:

"F₄ is the successor of F₃"

is a claim.

It is not automatically proof.

Continuity requires evidence concerning:

governance continuity
membership continuity
constitutional authority
federative obligations
provenance continuity
protocol continuity
identity continuity

TRIAS determines whether the claimed continuity is valid.


---

VI. 🏛️ EVOLUTION ≠ REPLACEMENT

R7.04 establishes:

EVOLUTION
=
CONTINUITY
+
CONTROLLED CHANGE

rather than:

EVOLUTION
=
DELETE OLD
+
INSTALL NEW

Thus:

F₃
 ↓
MIGRATION
 ↓
F₄

retains the causal relationship between both states.


---

VII. 🔄 MIGRATION PLAN

Every material constitutional evolution requires a migration plan.

Conceptually:

FederationMigration {
