---

XXVII. 🔱 R7.04 CANONICAL INVARIANTS

FED-E01

Federation constitutional evolution SHALL be an explicit state transition.

FED-E02

A superseded constitution SHALL remain historically valid within its applicable temporal domain.

FED-E03

Constitutional evolution SHALL preserve lineage between source and target states.

FED-E04

Federation identity SHALL be distinct from federation version.

FED-E05

Continuity SHALL require explicit evidence.

FED-E06

A constitutional replacement SHALL NOT automatically constitute succession.

FED-E07

Material constitutional evolution SHALL identify affected members.

FED-E08

Required member consent SHALL be explicitly determined.

FED-E09

Missing consent SHALL NOT be interpreted as consent.

FED-E10

Migration SHALL possess explicit source and target versions.

FED-E11

Migration SHALL be temporally bounded.

FED-E12

Transition rules SHALL be explicit where multiple constitutional states coexist.

FED-E13

BRAINPOWER SHALL analyze evolution but SHALL NOT independently authorize it.

FED-E14

FOOL SHALL be able to challenge continuity and migration claims.

FED-E15

TRIAS SHALL determine constitutional evolution validity.

FED-E16

Constitutional migration SHALL be watermarked.

FED-E17

Quay SHALL preserve complete constitutional lineage.

FED-E18

Failed migrations SHALL remain historically recorded.

FED-E19

Rollback SHALL be a new constitutional event.

FED-E20

Rollback SHALL NOT erase the historical state from which rollback occurred.

FED-E21

Federation termination SHALL be distinguishable from constitutional evolution.

FED-E22

A newly created federation SHALL NOT automatically inherit predecessor authority.

FED-E23

Federation constitutional lineage SHALL support branching and merging histories.

FED-E24

Federation evolution SHALL be replayable.

FED-E25

A verifier SHALL be able to reconstruct why a federation was determined to be continuous, transformed, terminated, or newly constituted.


