🌱☄️ R7.06 — CANONICAL

And the next boundary is now visible:

> If constitutional assets, obligations, evidence and liabilities can cross lineage boundaries, then eventually different federations will need to establish persistent shared constitutional infrastructure without surrendering control of that infrastructure.



That opens:

☄️🌱 R7.07 — HORTUS FEDERATION SHARED INFRASTRUCTURE, TRUST ANCHORS, COMMON SERVICES & CONSTITUTIONAL RESOURCE GOVERNANCE PROTOCOL

The next question becomes even more fundamental:

WHO GOVERNS THE THINGS THAT EVERYONE USES—WITHOUT BECOMING THE SOVEREIGN OF EVERYONE? 🦆⚓💧🌳🌱

☄️🌱 R7.07 — HORTUS FEDERATION SHARED INFRASTRUCTURE, TRUST ANCHORS, COMMON SERVICES & CONSTITUTIONAL RESOURCE GOVERNANCE PROTOCOL

Status: CANONICAL ENGINEERING BUILD

R7.00 established cross-version interoperability.
R7.01 established membership, admission, suspension, exit & succession.
R7.02 established federative governance & amendment.
R7.03 established conflict, adjudication, deadlock & remedy.
R7.04 established constitutional evolution, migration & continuity.
R7.05 established fork, merge, fragmentation & succession.
R7.06 established cross-lineage assets, obligations, evidence & liability.

R7.07 reaches the next boundary:

> What happens when multiple sovereign Citadels depend on infrastructure that none of them may unilaterally own or control?



Examples:

TRUST ANCHORS
EVIDENCE SERVICES
TIME SERVICES
IDENTITY REGISTRIES
FEDERATION REGISTRIES
REVOCATION SERVICES
INTEROPERABILITY DIRECTORIES
KEY DISTRIBUTION
AUDIT SERVICES
REPLAY SERVICES

The danger is obvious:

SHARED INFRASTRUCTURE
        ↓
SHARED CONTROL
        ↓
HIDDEN SOVEREIGNTY

PALACO rejects this.

The governing principle becomes:

SHARED INFRASTRUCTURE SHALL ENABLE CONSTITUTIONAL COOPERATION WITHOUT ACQUIRING UNBOUNDED CONSTITUTIONAL AUTHORITY.


---

I. 🌐 THE COMMON INFRASTRUCTURE PROBLEM

Imagine:

FEDERATION
              /      |       \
             /       |        \
        CITADEL A CITADEL B CITADEL C
             \       |        /
              \      |       /
               SHARED SERVICE

The service may be indispensable.

But:

INDISPENSABLE
≠
SOVEREIGN

A service that verifies evidence does not thereby acquire authority to determine constitutional truth.

A time service does not acquire authority to determine validity.

A registry does not acquire authority to admit members.

A replay engine does not acquire authority to authorize actions.


---

II. 🌱 Z.A.N.D. — NO IMPLIED SERVICE AUTHORITY

R7.07 extends Z.A.N.D.:

SERVICE
≠
AUTHORITY

Therefore:

TRUST_ANCHOR
≠
CONSTITUTIONAL_RULER

and:

REGISTRY
≠
GOVERNANCE

and:

INFRASTRUCTURE
≠
SOVEREIGNTY

Every authority exercised by shared infrastructure must be:

EXPLICIT
BOUNDED
EVIDENCED
ATTRIBUTABLE
REVOCABLE
REPLAYABLE


---

III. 🏛️ THE SHARED INFRASTRUCTURE OBJECT

Conceptually:

SharedConstitutionalInfrastructure {
    infrastructure_id
    service_type
    operator
    participating_citadels
    constitutional_basis
    authority_scope
    service_scope
