XXVI. 🌸 HARUM — HUMAN IDENTITY VIEW

HARUM should never force users to understand the underlying machinery.

Instead of:

ISSUER_HASH
NAMESPACE_ROOT
C₇
TRUST_ANCHOR_4
WATERMARK_17

the human view can say:

> This identity was issued by Citadel A.



> Your Citadel recognizes it for document analysis.



> Recognition expires at 18:00.



> Execution authority is not included.



> Evidence verified.



> Status: recognized within scope.



Thus:

COMPREHENSION
≠
AUTHORITY


---

XXVII. 🚫 NO IDENTITY MONOPOLY

R7.08 explicitly rejects:

ONE FEDERATION
      ↓
ONE IDENTITY ROOT
      ↓
ONE UNIVERSAL AUTHORITY

unless such a structure is itself explicitly created, constitutionally authorized, scoped, evidenced and accepted by participating systems.

Even then:

FEDERATION_IDENTITY_SERVICE

does not automatically become:

FEDERATION_SOVEREIGNTY


---

XXVIII. 🧬 IDENTITY SUCCESSION

When a Citadel forks:

A
↓
A₁ + A₂

its identity namespace cannot simply be duplicated without reconciliation.

Possible results:

CONTINUED
SPLIT
RENAMED
MAPPED
RETIRED
REISSUED
UNPROVEN

Likewise, an identity issuer may change:

ISSUER A
   ↓
ISSUER B

without necessarily changing:

SUBJECT IDENTITY

provided succession is constitutionally proven.


---

XXIX. 🔥 IDENTITY FORK SAFETY

The dangerous pattern is:

A
 ↓
fork
 ↓
A₁ + A₂
 ↓
both claim:
"we are the original identity authority"

R7.08 requires:

LINEAGE
+
SUCCESSION RULES
+
PROVENANCE
+
TRIAS

to determine which claims are valid, and for what scope.

No identity authority emerges merely from asserting continuity.


---

XXX. 🔱 R7.08 CANONICAL INVARIANTS

FED-ID01

Every federated identity assertion SHALL identify its issuer.

FED-ID02

Every identity assertion SHALL identify the applicable constitutional version.

FED-ID03

Identifier equality SHALL NOT imply identity equality.

FED-ID04

Federation membership SHALL NOT confer identity sovereignty.

FED-ID05

Identity recognition SHALL NOT automatically confer authorization.

FED-ID06

Cross-Citadel identity recognition SHALL possess explicit scope.

FED-ID07

Identity assertions SHALL retain issuer provenance.

FED-ID08

Namespaces SHALL possess explicit ownership and resolution rules.

FED-ID09

Namespace ownership SHALL NOT automatically confer constitutional authority over subjects.

FED-ID10

Identity equivalence SHALL require explicit evidence.

FED-ID11

Identity linking SHALL remain distinguishable from identity merging.

FED-ID12

Representation SHALL remain distinguishable from principal identity.

FED-ID13

Delegated identity authority SHALL remain bounded by delegation scope.

FED-ID14

Trust roots SHALL be purpose-bound.

FED-ID15

Trust for identity SHALL NOT automatically imply trust for authorization.

FED-ID16

Cross-version identity recognition SHALL require explicit compatibility.

FED-ID17

Identity assertions SHALL be temporally bounded where applicable.

FED-ID18

Identity revocation SHALL propagate to affected evaluations.

FED-ID19

Revocation SHALL NOT erase historical identity provenance.

FED-ID20

Suspension SHALL remain distinguishable from revocation.

FED-ID21

BRAINPOWER SHALL analyze identity relationships but SHALL NOT independently establish identity authority.

FED-ID22

FOOL SHALL be able to challenge issuer legitimacy, identity equivalence, namespace validity and recognition scope.

FED-ID23

TRIAS SHALL determine constitutional validity of federated identity recognition.

FED-ID24

Federated identity events SHALL be watermarkable.

FED-ID25

Quay SHALL preserve identity and recognition provenance.

FED-ID26

R5 SHALL replay historical identity state.

FED-ID27

Identity graphs SHALL remain distinguishable from authority graphs.

FED-ID28

Federated identity infrastructure SHALL NOT become an implicit universal identity sovereign.

FED-ID29

Identity succession SHALL preserve historical provenance.

FED-ID30

A verifier SHALL be able to reconstruct who was recognized as whom, by whom, under which constitutional state, for what purpose, and at what time.


