VALID
AUTHORIZED
DENIED
REPLAYED
EXPIRED
REVOKED
OUT_OF_SCOPE
EFFECT_MISMATCH
CONFLICTED
UNPROVEN


---

XX. 🔄 REPLAY ATTACKS

A valid message from:

10:00

must not automatically be reusable at:

15:00

Therefore messages may require:

NONCE
MESSAGE_ID
SEQUENCE
EXPIRATION
AUDIENCE
TEMPORAL_SCOPE

A message valid in:

CITADEL B

must not automatically become valid in:

CITADEL C


---

XXI. 🎯 AUDIENCE BINDING

A cross-Citadel message can be bound to:

sender
receiver
federation
purpose
scope
time

Thus:

MESSAGE_FOR_B

cannot silently become:

MESSAGE_FOR_C

This closes a subtle authority-transfer channel.


---

XXII. 🚫 NO MESSAGE REUSE

R7.09 establishes:

> A message SHALL NOT be reusable outside its proven audience, scope or temporal validity merely because its cryptographic integrity remains intact.



Therefore:

SIGNATURE_VALID

is insufficient.

The verifier must also establish:

AUDIENCE_VALID
SCOPE_VALID
TIME_VALID
PURPOSE_VALID


---

XXIII. 🌐 CROSS-VERSION MESSAGE SEMANTICS

Suppose:

A → C₇
B → C₈

A sends:

ACTION_CODE = 17

But C₇ and C₈ interpret 17 differently.

Then:

IDENTITY_VALID
MESSAGE_VALID

may both be true while:

SEMANTIC_COMPATIBILITY = FALSE

R7.09 therefore requires explicit semantic interoperability.

This is crucial.

PROTOCOL COMPATIBILITY IS NOT MESSAGE COMPATIBILITY.


---

XXIV. 🧬 SEMANTIC CONTRACT

The federated message may therefore reference:

SemanticContract {
    contract_id
    message_version
    schema_version
    action_semantics
    field_semantics
    effect_model
    error_model
    compatibility_rules
    temporal_validity
    provenance
}

This ensures that:

same bytes

do not accidentally mean:

different actions


---

XXV. 🌱 NO SEMANTIC ASSUMPTION

Z.A.N.D. now operates at three levels:

IDENTITY ASSUMPTION = NONE
AUTHORITY ASSUMPTION = NONE
SEMANTIC ASSUMPTION = NONE

Therefore:

> A receiver SHALL NOT infer the meaning of a cross-version action merely from a familiar identifier, field, command name or historical convention.




---

XXVI. 🚨 EFFECT BOUNDARY

The most important implementation boundary becomes:

REQUESTED_EFFECT
        ↓
AUTHORIZED_EFFECT
        ↓
ACTUAL_EFFECT

All three must be distinguishable.

Example:

REQUESTED = ANALYZE
AUTHORIZED = ANALYZE
ACTUAL = ANALYZE + EXPORT

Then:

EFFECT_MISMATCH

The extra effect cannot be hidden inside implementation detail.


---

