XXXI. 🔱 R7.09 CANONICAL INVARIANTS

FED-M01

A message SHALL NOT itself constitute constitutional authority.

FED-M02

Identity SHALL remain distinct from message authority.

FED-M03

Intent SHALL remain distinct from authorization.

FED-M04

A request SHALL remain distinguishable from a command.

FED-M05

Cross-Citadel messages SHALL identify their sender and intended receiver.

FED-M06

Message validity SHALL be distinct from action authorization.

FED-M07

Federated capabilities SHALL possess explicit scope.

FED-M08

Capabilities SHALL retain originating authority provenance.

FED-M09

Sub-delegated capability SHALL NOT exceed originating delegated scope.

FED-M10

Message audiences SHALL be explicit.

FED-M11

Message temporal validity SHALL be explicit where applicable.

FED-M12

Message replay SHALL be detectable or prevented according to the applicable protocol.

FED-M13

Cross-version message semantics SHALL be explicitly established.

FED-M14

Identical message identifiers SHALL NOT imply identical semantics across constitutional versions.

FED-M15

Declared intent SHALL remain distinguishable from actual effects.

FED-M16

Actual effects SHALL NOT silently exceed authorized effects.

FED-M17

Cryptographic authenticity SHALL NOT automatically establish authorization.

FED-M18

BRAINPOWER SHALL analyze intent, capability, semantics and effect models but SHALL NOT independently authorize execution.

FED-M19

FOOL SHALL be able to challenge identity, authority, delegation, capability, semantics, audience and effect boundaries.

FED-M20

TRIAS SHALL determine cross-Citadel action validity.

FED-M21

Federated message events SHALL be watermarkable.

FED-M22

Quay SHALL preserve complete message-to-action provenance.

FED-M23

R5 SHALL replay historical message, authority and capability state.

FED-M24

Revocation SHALL affect future use of revoked capabilities according to their applicable temporal semantics.

FED-M25

Historical validity SHALL NOT be retroactively altered merely by current identity or capability state.

FED-M26

A message valid for one audience SHALL NOT automatically be valid for another audience.

FED-M27

A message valid under one constitutional version SHALL NOT automatically be valid under another.

FED-M28

Cross-Citadel communication SHALL NOT silently amplify authority.

FED-M29

Service-side effects SHALL remain within the proven constitutional effect boundary.

FED-M30

A verifier SHALL be able to reconstruct who sent what, with what intent, under which authority and delegation, to whom, under which version and scope, producing which actual effects and why the resulting action was valid or invalid.


---

XXXII. ☄️ THE R7.09 ACTION EQUATION

Conceptually:

VALID FEDERATED ACTION
=
VALID IDENTITY
∩
VALID MESSAGE
∩
VALID INTENT
∩
VALID AUTHORITY
∩
VALID DELEGATION
∩
VALID CAPABILITY
∩
SEMANTIC COMPATIBILITY
∩
VALID AUDIENCE
∩
VALID SCOPE
∩
VALID TIME
∩
VALID EFFECT BOUNDARY

Then:

BRAINPOWER
 ↓
FOOL
 ↓
TRIAS
 ↓
WATERMARK
 ↓
QUAY
 ↓
R5


---

XXXIII. 🌱 THE HORTUS COMMUNICATION PRINCIPLE

R7.09 establishes:

> A recognized identity may communicate without thereby acquiring authority.



> A message may express intent without thereby becoming authorization.



> A capability may cross a boundary without expanding beyond its proven scope.



> A valid signature may establish authenticity without establishing constitutional legitimacy.



And the strongest formulation:

COMMUNICATION MAY CROSS A SOVEREIGN BOUNDARY; AUTHORITY MAY CROSS ONLY THROUGH PROVEN CONSTITUTIONAL MECHANISM.


---

