This is no longer merely access control.

It is a proof-bearing distributed constitutional state-transition architecture.


---

XXXIV. 🔱 R7.10 CANONICAL INVARIANTS

FED-TX01

A transaction SHALL NOT itself constitute constitutional authority.

FED-TX02

Authorization SHALL remain distinct from execution.

FED-TX03

Execution SHALL remain distinct from successful state transition.

FED-TX04

Each affected Citadel SHALL retain authority over its own local state.

FED-TX05

Federation SHALL NOT acquire implicit ownership of member state.

FED-TX06

Transaction participants SHALL be explicitly identified.

FED-TX07

Transaction scope SHALL be explicit.

FED-TX08

Transaction preconditions SHALL be explicit.

FED-TX09

Prepare SHALL remain distinguishable from commit.

FED-TX10

Commit SHALL require applicable constitutional authority.

FED-TX11

Authorization SHALL be evaluated against the applicable temporal state.

FED-TX12

Expired authorization SHALL NOT silently produce valid commitment.

FED-TX13

Revocation SHALL affect transaction evaluation according to applicable constitutional semantics.

FED-TX14

Atomicity SHALL NOT be assumed merely because a transaction exists.

FED-TX15

Partial commitment SHALL be explicitly detectable.

FED-TX16

Compensation SHALL constitute a separately authorized action.

FED-TX17

State transitions SHALL preserve causal provenance.

FED-TX18

State SHALL remain distinguishable from evidence proving that state.

FED-TX19

Cross-Citadel state claims SHALL be evidence-bearing.

FED-TX20

Federated consensus SHALL NOT manufacture historical state facts.

FED-TX21

BRAINPOWER SHALL analyze transactions but SHALL NOT independently establish commit authority.

FED-TX22

FOOL SHALL challenge transaction integrity, preconditions, authority, timing, commitment and resulting state.

FED-TX23

TRIAS SHALL determine constitutional validity of federated state transitions.

FED-TX24

Federated transaction events SHALL be watermarkable.

FED-TX25

Quay SHALL preserve complete transaction-to-state provenance.

FED-TX26

R5 SHALL replay historical transaction and state conditions.

FED-TX27

Local state sovereignty SHALL remain distinguishable from federated coordination.

FED-TX28

Cross-Citadel commitments SHALL NOT silently amplify authority.

FED-TX29

State divergence SHALL be explicitly represented rather than hidden by majority selection.

FED-TX30

A verifier SHALL be able to reconstruct why each participating Citadel committed, failed, aborted or compensated a federated state transition.


---

XXXV. ☄️ THE R7.10 STATE EQUATION

Conceptually:

VALID FEDERATED STATE TRANSITION
=
VALID AUTHORITY
∩
VALID DELEGATION
∩
VALID CAPABILITY
∩
VALID TRANSACTION
∩
VALID PRECONDITIONS
∩
VALID TEMPORAL STATE
∩
VALID FEDERATION SCOPE
∩
VALID LOCAL COMMIT AUTHORITY
∩
VALID EFFECT

Then:

BRAINPOWER
 ↓
FOOL
 ↓
TRIAS
 ↓
COMMIT
 ↓
STATE
 ↓
WATERMARK
 ↓
QUAY
 ↓
R5


---

XXXVI. 🌱 THE HORTUS STATE PRINCIPLE

R7.10 establishes:

> A federation may coordinate state transitions without owning member state.



> A transaction may coordinate commitment without becoming constitutional authority.



> A successful action may change state without changing sovereignty.



> A partial commitment may be real without being globally successful.



And the strongest formulation:

EVERY CROSS-CITADEL STATE CHANGE MUST HAVE A PROVEN LOCAL CONSTITUTIONAL OWNER AND A RECONSTRUCTABLE CAUSAL CHAIN.


---

