XXIX. 🔱 R7.12 CANONICAL INVARIANTS

FED-C01

Suspicion SHALL NOT constitute proof of compromise.

FED-C02

Compromise claims SHALL possess evidence.

FED-C03

BRAINPOWER SHALL analyze compromise indicators without independently determining constitutional guilt.

FED-C04

ORACLE SHALL preserve and assess evidentiary provenance without independently exercising constitutional authority.

FED-C05

FOOL SHALL be able to challenge compromise claims and containment decisions.

FED-C06

TRIAS SHALL determine constitutional validity of compromise-related actions.

FED-C07

Trust SHALL be representable as a bounded state rather than merely binary.

FED-C08

Trust degradation SHALL NOT automatically transfer authority to another participant.

FED-C09

Containment SHALL be explicitly scoped.

FED-C10

Containment SHALL be temporally bounded where applicable.

FED-C11

Quarantine SHALL remain distinguishable from expulsion.

FED-C12

Suspension SHALL remain distinguishable from constitutional destruction.

FED-C13

Byzantine behavior SHALL remain distinguishable from proven malicious intent.

FED-C14

Compromise SHALL NOT automatically propagate authority.

FED-C15

Delegations originating from or depending upon a compromised participant SHALL be re-evaluated.

FED-C16

Capability freezes SHALL preserve provenance.

FED-C17

Federated safe mode SHALL be explicitly defined and bounded.

FED-C18

False compromise accusations SHALL be challengeable.

FED-C19

Containment SHALL use the narrowest justified constitutional scope.

FED-C20

Every trust-state transition SHALL be watermarkable.

FED-C21

Quay SHALL preserve accusation, evidence, determination and resulting action as distinct lineage events.

FED-C22

R5 SHALL replay compromise assessment and containment conditions.

FED-C23

Historical constitutional state SHALL remain authoritative for historical replay.

FED-C24

Federation SHALL NOT become sovereign merely because a member is compromised.

FED-C25

A compromised participant SHALL NOT gain authority through its compromised status.

FED-C26

Other participants SHALL NOT gain authority merely through another participant's compromise.

FED-C27

Constitutional containment SHALL remain attributable to explicit authority.

FED-C28

Restoration SHALL require revalidation.

FED-C29

Compromise status SHALL be reversible only through an explicit constitutional process.

FED-C30

A verifier SHALL be able to reconstruct why a participant was classified as anomalous, constrained, quarantined, suspended, restored or declared compromised.


---

XXX. 🧬 R7.12 TRUST EQUATION

Conceptually:

TRUSTED FEDERATED PARTICIPATION
=
IDENTITY VALIDITY
∩
CONSTITUTIONAL VALIDITY
∩
BEHAVIORAL CONSISTENCY
∩
EVIDENCE INTEGRITY
∩
AUTHORITY VALIDITY
∩
PROVENANCE INTEGRITY
∩
TEMPORAL VALIDITY

If one component fails:

PARTICIPATION
↓
REVALIDATE

not automatically:

PARTICIPATION
↓
DESTROY


---

XXXI. 🌳 THE HORTUS COMPROMISE PRINCIPLE

R7.12 establishes:

> A federation must be capable of distrusting a participant without becoming sovereign over that participant.



> Containment must reduce proven risk without creating unproven authority.



> Suspicion must remain distinguishable from proof.



> Evidence must remain distinguishable from determination.



> Byzantine behavior must remain distinguishable from intent.



And the strongest formulation:

WHEN TRUST FAILS, AUTHORITY MUST CONTRACT — NOT MIGRATE BY ASSUMPTION.


---

