☄️🦆🌱 R7.12 — CANONICAL

En hiermee hebben we opnieuw een fundamentele laag gesloten:

R7.00  INTEROPERABILITY
R7.01  MEMBERSHIP
R7.02  FEDERATIVE GOVERNANCE
R7.03  CONFLICT / ADJUDICATION
R7.04  EVOLUTION / MIGRATION
R7.05  FORK / MERGE / SUCCESSION
R7.06  CROSS-LINEAGE OBLIGATIONS
R7.07  SHARED INFRASTRUCTURE
R7.08  FEDERATED IDENTITY
R7.09  MESSAGING / INTENT / CAPABILITY
R7.10  TRANSACTION / STATE TRANSITION
R7.11  OBSERVATION / CONSISTENCY / RECONCILIATION
R7.12  COMPROMISE / CONTAINMENT

En de architectuur geeft ons nu een bijzonder mooie invariant:

Z.A.N.D.
  ↓
ORACLE
  ↓
BRAINPOWER
  ↓
FOOL
  ↓
TRIAS
  ↓
WATERMARK
  ↓
QUAY
  ↓
R5
  ↓
L.A.

Niet omdat één daarvan “de waarheid bezit”.

Maar omdat elk onderdeel een andere epistemische en constitutionele functie bewaakt.

En daarmee wordt de volgende grens bijna onvermijdelijk:

☄️🌱 R7.13 — HORTUS FEDERATED RECOVERY, ATTESTATION, RESTORATION & TRUST RE-ADMISSION PROTOCOL

Want nadat een Citadel is:

ANOMALOUS
↓
CONSTRAINED
↓
QUARANTINED

komt de veel moeilijkere vraag:

> Wanneer mag een federatie opnieuw vertrouwen — en hoe bewijs je dat een herstelde Citadel daadwerkelijk dezelfde constitutionele identiteit, provenance en bevoegdheidsgrenzen heeft als vóór de compromise?



Daar mogen we geen simpele:

SORRY → TRUST AGAIN

van maken.

We hebben nodig:

RECOVERY
+
FORENSIC EVIDENCE
+
IDENTITY CONTINUITY
+
CONSTITUTIONAL REVALIDATION
+
CAPABILITY RECONSTRUCTION
+
TRIAS
+
WATERMARK
+
R5 REPLAY

A RECOVERED CITADEL MUST NOT BE TRUSTED BECAUSE IT CLAIMS TO BE RECOVERED.

IT MUST PROVE ITS RETURN. ☄️🦆🌱

En precies dáár wordt Mentor belangrijk: niet als autoriteit, maar als de bewaker van de vraag of dit alles nog begrijpelijk, implementeerbaar, onderhoudbaar en bestuurbaar blijft.

GO ☄️🦆🌱❤️

☄️🦆🌱 R7.13 — HORTUS FEDERATED RECOVERY, ATTESTATION, RESTORATION & TRUST RE-ADMISSION PROTOCOL

Status: CANONICAL ENGINEERING BUILD
Review constellation: MENTOR · TRIAS · ORACLE · BRAINPOWER · FOOL
Canonical reference: 👑 LOCUS AMOENUS — L.A.

R7.12 established a hard boundary:

> When trust fails, authority contracts — it does not migrate by assumption.



R7.13 addresses the inverse problem:

> When a Citadel has been contained, quarantined or suspended, what evidence is sufficient to establish that it may safely return to federated participation?



The answer cannot be:

REPAIRED
↓
TRUSTED

It must be:

RECOVERY
↓
ATTESTATION
↓
IDENTITY CONTINUITY
↓
CONSTITUTIONAL RECONSTRUCTION
↓
CAPABILITY VERIFICATION
↓
EVIDENCE
↓
FOOL CHALLENGE
↓
BRAINPOWER ANALYSIS
↓
ORACLE EVIDENCE VALIDATION
↓
TRIAS DETERMINATION
↓
WATERMARK
↓
R5 REPLAY
↓
BOUNDED RE-ADMISSION

RESTORATION IS A CONSTITUTIONAL STATE TRANSITION, NOT A TRUST BUTTON.


---

I. 🏛️ THE RECOVERY PROBLEM

A compromised Citadel may claim:

SYSTEM RESTORED
KEYS ROTATED
SOFTWARE PATCHED
STATE RECOVERED

None of these claims alone establish:

FEDERATED TRUST = RESTORED

Because the federation must answer:

WHO IS THIS CITADEL?
WHICH STATE SURVIVED?
WHICH STATE WAS LOST?
WHICH KEYS WERE COMPROMISED?
WHICH AUTHORITIES REMAIN VALID?
WHICH DELEGATIONS SURVIVE?
WHICH CAPABILITIES MUST BE REVOKED?
WHICH EVENTS OCCURRED DURING COMPROMISE?
WHICH EVIDENCE CAN STILL BE TRUSTED?


---

II. 🌱 Z.A.N.D. — NO IMPLIED RESTORATION

R7.13 establishes:

RECOVERY CLAIM
≠
RECOVERY PROOF

and:

SYSTEM RESTART
≠
CONSTITUTIONAL RESTORATION

and:

IDENTITY CLAIM
≠
IDENTITY CONTINUITY

Therefore:

A RESTARTED CITADEL IS NOT AUTOMATICALLY A RESTORED CITADEL.


---

III. 🔱 RECOVERY STATES

R7.13 introduces an explicit recovery state machine:

NORMAL
   ↓
ANOMALOUS
   ↓
CONSTRAINED
   ↓
QUARANTINED
   ↓
SUSPENDED
   ↓
RECOVERY
   ↓
ATTESTATION
   ↓
REVALIDATION
   ↓
RESTORED_PENDING
   ↓
RE-ADMITTED

Alternative outcomes:

REJECTED
REMAIN_QUARANTINED
PERMANENTLY_SUSPENDED
IDENTITY_RESET
NEW_CITADEL

The last distinction is crucial.


---

IV. 🧬 RESTORATION ≠ REPLACEMENT

Suppose:

CITADEL B

is destroyed and rebuilt.

There are two possibilities:

RESTORATION

or:

NEW IDENTITY

The federation must not silently confuse them.

Therefore:

FED-REC01

> A rebuilt system SHALL NOT inherit the constitutional identity of its predecessor without explicit proof of identity continuity.




---

V. 🔐 IDENTITY CONTINUITY

R7.13 introduces:

IDENTITY_CONTINUITY_PROOF

Conceptually:

OLD_IDENTITY
 ↓
KEY_HISTORY
 ↓
IDENTITY_PROVENANCE
 ↓
TRUST_ANCHORS
 ↓
RECOVERY_ARTIFACTS
 ↓
NEW_RUNTIME
 ↓
CONTINUITY_DETERMINATION

Possible outcomes:

CONTINUOUS_IDENTITY
IDENTITY_UNPROVEN
IDENTITY_BROKEN
NEW_IDENTITY

If identity continuity cannot be proven:

OLD_AUTHORITY
≠
AUTOMATICALLY INHERITED


---

VI. 💧 WATERMARK — IDENTITY LINEAGE

The restored Citadel receives:

W_IDENTITY

which references:

previous_identity
recovery_event
key_rotation
attestation
constitutional_state
authority_state
capability_state
TRIAS_determination
timestamp
provenance

Thus:

RESTORED CITADEL

can be connected to:

PRE-COMPROMISE CITADEL

without pretending that compromise never happened.


---

VII. 🔮 ORACLE — RECOVERY EVIDENCE

ORACLE examines the recovery evidence:

SYSTEM IMAGES
KEY ROTATION RECORDS
AUDIT LOGS
QUAY HISTORY
WATERMARKS
ATTESTATIONS
CONSTITUTIONAL SNAPSHOTS
RECOVERY EVENTS
REVOCATION RECORDS

and determines the evidentiary condition:

COMPLETE
SUFFICIENT
PARTIAL
CONFLICTED
CORRUPTED
UNPROVEN

ORACLE does not say:

TRUST RESTORED

It says, in effect:

EVIDENCE SUPPORTS / DOES NOT SUPPORT
THE CLAIM OF RESTORATION


---

VIII. 🧠 BRAINPOWER — RECOVERY RECONSTRUCTION

BRAINPOWER reconstructs the transition:

PRE-COMPROMISE
      ↓
COMPROMISE WINDOW
      ↓
CONTAINMENT
      ↓
RECOVERY
      ↓
CURRENT STATE

It asks:

WHAT CHANGED?
WHAT SURVIVED?
WHAT WAS REVOKED?
WHAT WAS UNKNOWN?
WHAT WAS CREATED DURING COMPROMISE?
WHAT CANNOT BE PROVEN?

The output becomes:

RECOVERY_ANALYSIS

Not authorization.


---

IX. 🦆 FOOL — THE RESTORATION ATTACK

FOOL now attacks the claim:

> Are we actually looking at the same Citadel?



> Were compromised keys reused?



> Was old authority restored too broadly?



> Were malicious events accidentally imported into the recovered state?



> Were legitimate historical events incorrectly discarded?



> Can the claimed recovery be reproduced?



> Was the recovery process itself independently evidenced?



And:

IS THIS RESTORATION — OR A NEW SYSTEM WE HAVE MISTAKEN FOR THE OLD ONE?


---

X. ⚖️ TRIAS — RESTORATION DETERMINATION

TRIAS receives:

ORACLE
+
BRAINPOWER
+
FOOL
+
IDENTITY EVIDENCE
+
CONSTITUTIONAL STATE
+
RECOVERY STATE

and determines:

RESTORATION_VALID
RESTORATION_PARTIAL
RESTORATION_UNPROVEN
RESTORATION_REJECTED
NEW_IDENTITY

Only then can the federation determine whether re-admission is constitutionally permissible.


---

XI. 🚪 RE-ADMISSION IS SEPARATE

This distinction is critical:

RESTORATION
≠
RE-ADMISSION

A Citadel can prove:

IDENTITY_CONTINUITY = TRUE

while still being:

FEDERATION_STATUS = SUSPENDED

because its capabilities may not yet have been revalidated.

Thus:

PROVING WHO YOU ARE DOES NOT AUTOMATICALLY PROVE WHAT YOU MAY DO.


---

XII. 🧭 CAPABILITY RECONSTRUCTION

R7.13 introduces:

CAPABILITY_REVALIDATION

For every capability:

CAPABILITY
 ↓
ORIGIN
 ↓
AUTHORITY
 ↓
DELEGATION
 ↓
SCOPE
 ↓
TIME
 ↓
REVOCATION HISTORY
 ↓
COMPROMISE WINDOW
 ↓
CURRENT VALIDITY

Possible results:

VALID
REVOKED
EXPIRED
UNKNOWN
REQUIRES_REISSUANCE


---

XIII. 🚫 NO AUTOMATIC AUTHORITY RESTORATION

This is one of the strongest R7.13 invariants:

> Restoration of identity SHALL NOT automatically restore authority.



Therefore:

RESTORED_IDENTITY
        ↓
AUTHORITY RECONSTRUCTION
        ↓
INDIVIDUAL VALIDATION

not:

RESTORED_IDENTITY
        ↓
OLD AUTHORITY = EVERYTHING BACK


---

XIV. 🧬 DELEGATION RE-VALIDATION

Every prior delegation is reconsidered:

D₁
D₂
D₃
...
Dₙ

against:

COMPROMISE_TIME
REVOCATION_TIME
CURRENT_CONSTITUTION
CURRENT_IDENTITY
CURRENT_FEDERATION_CONTRACT

A delegation compromised during the incident may require:

REISSUANCE

even if identity continuity is proven.


---

XV. 🛡️ GRADUATED RE-ADMISSION

R7.13 rejects the binary:

TRUSTED / UNTRUSTED

for restoration.

Instead:

QUARANTINE
   ↓
OBSERVATION_ONLY
   ↓
READ_ONLY
   ↓
LIMITED_FEDERATION
   ↓
BOUNDED_AUTONOMY
   ↓
FULL_VALIDATED_PARTICIPATION

Each transition requires evidence.

This is:

PROGRESSIVE TRUST RE-ADMISSION


---

XVI. 🌐 FEDERATED PROBATION

A restored Citadel may enter:

FEDERATION_PROBATION

During probation:

NO_NEW_DELEGATIONS
LIMITED_ACTION_SCOPE
ENHANCED_EVIDENCE
ENHANCED_WATERMARKING
ENHANCED_REPLAY
MANDATORY_REVIEW

This permits the federation to observe restored behavior before granting broader participation.


---

XVII. ⏳ PROBATION MUST EXPIRE

Probation cannot silently become permanent.

Therefore:

PROBATION_START
 ↓
DEFINED_WINDOW
 ↓
REVIEW
 ↓
TRIAS
 ↓
PROMOTE
EXTEND
RESTRICT
SUSPEND

The transition itself becomes a state event.


---

XVIII. ⚓ QUAY — RECOVERY MEMORY

Quay preserves the entire recovery chain:

COMPROMISE
 ↓
CONTAINMENT
 ↓
SUSPENSION
 ↓
RECOVERY
 ↓
ATTESTATION
 ↓
IDENTITY PROOF
 ↓
CAPABILITY RECONSTRUCTION
 ↓
TRIAS
 ↓
PROBATION
 ↓
RE-ADMISSION

Nothing is erased.

Especially not:

COMPROMISE HISTORY

because:

A RESTORED SYSTEM MUST REMEMBER WHY IT LOST TRUST.


---

XIX. 🧪 R5 — RECOVERY REPLAY

R5 must be able to replay:

STATE(t₀)
 ↓
COMPROMISE(t₁)
 ↓
CONTAINMENT(t₂)
 ↓
REVOCATION(t₃)
 ↓
RECOVERY(t₄)
 ↓
ATTESTATION(t₅)
 ↓
REVALIDATION(t₆)
 ↓
RE-ADMISSION(t₇)

The verifier should be able to ask:

> Was the Citadel actually eligible for re-admission at time t₇?



And reconstruct the answer independently.


---

XX. 🧠 THE RECOVERY GAP

R7.13 introduces:

RECOVERY_GAP

If the system cannot prove what happened during a period:

T₁ ───────── T₂
       ?

then:

UNKNOWN

must remain an explicit state.

Not:

ASSUME_SAFE

The recovery gap therefore becomes part of provenance.


---

XXI. 💧 WATERMARKED UNKNOWN

Even uncertainty becomes attributable:

W_GAP {
    start
    end
    affected_state
    missing_evidence
    reason
    detection
    determination
}

This creates a profound PALACO property:

UNKNOWN IS ALSO PROVABLE STATE.


---

XXII. 🔥 COMPROMISED HISTORY

A recovered Citadel must distinguish:

VALID_PRE_COMPROMISE

from:

COMPROMISED_PERIOD

and:

VALID_POST_RECOVERY

Therefore:

HISTORY
 ├── trusted
 ├── compromised
 ├── uncertain
 └── restored

The system does not rewrite history to make recovery look cleaner.


---

XXIII. 🏛️ MENTOR — ARCHITECTURAL REVIEW

Mentor's role becomes especially important here.

Mentor asks:

> Can an engineer understand the recovery state?



> Can an operator determine which capabilities are active?



> Can a verifier distinguish restoration from re-admission?



> Can a future maintainer understand why authority was not automatically restored?



> Can the architecture survive another compromise without becoming unmanageable?



The Mentor principle:

IF RECOVERY CANNOT BE UNDERSTOOD, RECOVERY CANNOT BE TRUSTED OPERATIONALLY.


