XXVII. 🔱 R7.13 CANONICAL INVARIANTS

FED-R01

Recovery SHALL be a constitutional state transition.

FED-R02

A system restart SHALL NOT constitute automatic restoration.

FED-R03

Restoration claims SHALL require evidence.

FED-R04

Identity continuity SHALL be explicitly proven where required.

FED-R05

A rebuilt Citadel SHALL NOT inherit predecessor authority without valid continuity proof.

FED-R06

Restoration SHALL remain distinct from federation re-admission.

FED-R07

Identity restoration SHALL NOT automatically restore authority.

FED-R08

Capabilities SHALL be independently revalidated.

FED-R09

Delegations affected by compromise SHALL be re-evaluated.

FED-R10

Compromised capabilities SHALL NOT silently return.

FED-R11

Re-admission MAY be graduated.

FED-R12

Federated probation SHALL be explicit and bounded.

FED-R13

Probation SHALL be reviewable.

FED-R14

Recovery gaps SHALL remain explicit unknown state.

FED-R15

Historical compromise SHALL NOT be erased by restoration.

FED-R16

Recovery provenance SHALL be preserved.

FED-R17

ORACLE SHALL assess recovery evidence.

FED-R18

BRAINPOWER SHALL reconstruct recovery state and causal relationships.

FED-R19

FOOL SHALL challenge restoration and re-admission claims.

FED-R20

TRIAS SHALL determine constitutional restoration validity.

FED-R21

MENTOR SHALL evaluate recovery architecture for comprehensibility and maintainability.

FED-R22

WATERMARK SHALL identify recovery-state transitions.

FED-R23

QUAY SHALL preserve the complete recovery lineage.

FED-R24

R5 SHALL replay recovery and re-admission decisions.

FED-R25

Restoration SHALL NOT create authority previously absent.

FED-R26

Federation SHALL NOT acquire sovereign authority through restoration procedures.

FED-R27

Unknown recovery state SHALL NOT be silently converted into trusted state.

FED-R28

A recovered Citadel SHALL retain its compromise history.

FED-R29

Re-admission SHALL require explicit determination.

FED-R30

A verifier SHALL be able to reconstruct why a Citadel was restored, restricted, rejected, or re-admitted.


