XXV. 🔱 R7.14 CANONICAL INVARIANTS

FED-T01

Cryptographic identity SHALL be represented as lineage rather than merely a current key.

FED-T02

A key SHALL NOT itself constitute constitutional authority.

FED-T03

Key rotation SHALL be independently attributable.

FED-T04

Key rotation SHALL NOT automatically imply authority transfer.

FED-T05

Authority transfer SHALL NOT be inferred solely from key continuity.

FED-T06

Trust-root succession SHALL require explicit evidence.

FED-T07

A compromised root SHALL NOT automatically authorize its own successor.

FED-T08

Root succession SHALL preserve constitutional provenance.

FED-T09

Cryptographic authenticity SHALL NOT by itself establish constitutional validity.

FED-T10

Signature validity SHALL be evaluated temporally.

FED-T11

Revoked keys SHALL NOT silently regain validity.

FED-T12

Later trust relationships SHALL NOT silently rewrite historical validity.

FED-T13

Trust gaps SHALL remain explicit.

FED-T14

ORACLE SHALL evaluate trust-chain evidence.

FED-T15

BRAINPOWER SHALL analyze cryptographic lineage.

FED-T16

FOOL SHALL challenge trust-root assumptions.

FED-T17

TRIAS SHALL determine constitutional trust validity.

FED-T18

MENTOR SHALL review trust architecture for comprehensibility and resilience.

FED-T19

WATERMARK SHALL preserve cryptographic succession provenance.

FED-T20

QUAY SHALL preserve trust-root and key lineage.

FED-T21

R5 SHALL replay historical trust state.

FED-T22

Federation roots SHALL NOT automatically become member constitutional roots.

FED-T23

Member Citadels MAY maintain independent cryptographic roots.

FED-T24

Cross-Citadel interoperability SHALL NOT require identical trust roots unless explicitly required by the applicable contract.

FED-T25

Root succession SHALL be replayable.

FED-T26

Key succession SHALL be replayable.

FED-T27

Attestation chains SHALL be replayable.

FED-T28

Identity continuity SHALL remain distinct from authority continuity.

FED-T29

Cryptographic continuity SHALL remain distinct from constitutional continuity.

FED-T30

A verifier SHALL be able to reconstruct the trust basis of a federated action.


