---

XXVI. 🔱 R7.15 CANONICAL INVARIANTS

FED-L01

A constitutional lineage MAY fork.

FED-L02

A fork SHALL require explicit provenance.

FED-L03

A fork SHALL NOT automatically invalidate either resulting lineage.

FED-L04

A fork SHALL NOT automatically validate either resulting lineage.

FED-L05

Lineage identity SHALL remain explicit after a fork.

FED-L06

Parallel constitutional validity SHALL be possible.

FED-L07

Parallel validity SHALL NOT permit overlapping contradictory authority without resolution.

FED-L08

A merge SHALL preserve both parent lineages.

FED-L09

A merge SHALL NOT erase historical divergence.

FED-L10

A merge SHALL require explicit authority.

FED-L11

A merge SHALL NOT automatically combine authority.

FED-L12

Reconciliation SHALL NOT require forced constitutional uniformity.

FED-L13

Historical states SHALL remain distinguishable from reconciled states.

FED-L14

Federation splits SHALL preserve predecessor history.

FED-L15

Federation merges SHALL explicitly define succession.

FED-L16

ORACLE SHALL validate lineage evidence.

FED-L17

BRAINPOWER SHALL analyze lineage graphs.

FED-L18

FOOL SHALL challenge fork and merge legitimacy.

FED-L19

TRIAS SHALL determine constitutional lineage validity.

FED-L20

MENTOR SHALL ensure branched history remains understandable.

FED-L21

WATERMARK SHALL preserve fork and merge provenance.

FED-L22

QUAY SHALL preserve branched provenance.

FED-L23

R5 SHALL replay branch-specific historical states.

FED-L24

R5 SHALL replay merged states.

FED-L25

Lineage selection SHALL be temporally explicit.

FED-L26

A lineage SHALL NOT silently inherit another lineage's authority.

FED-L27

A federation fork SHALL NOT automatically duplicate all federative authority.

FED-L28

A federation merge SHALL NOT automatically erase prior obligations.

FED-L29

Conflicting valid lineages SHALL remain distinguishable until explicitly reconciled.

FED-L30

A verifier SHALL be able to reconstruct the complete ancestry of a constitutional state.


---

XXVII. ☄️ THE R7.15 LINEAGE EQUATION

Conceptueel:

CONSTITUTIONAL STATE
=
ANCESTRY
+
LINEAGE
+
VERSION
+
AUTHORITY
+
SCOPE
+
TIME
+
EVIDENCE

Bij een fork:

PARENT
↓
FORK
↓
LINEAGE_A ∥ LINEAGE_B

Bij een merge:

LINEAGE_A
      \
       MERGE
      /
LINEAGE_B
      ↓
NEW_LINEAGE

Maar:

HISTORY(A)
+
HISTORY(B)
≠
ERASED_HISTORY

De geschiedenis blijft bestaan.


---

XXVIII. 🌱 THE DEEPER HORTUS PRINCIPLE

R7.15 maakt een belangrijk filosofisch punt technisch uitvoerbaar:

> Een levende constitutionele ecologie hoeft niet monolithisch te zijn om coherent te blijven.



Er kunnen:

VERSIONS
BRANCHES
FEDERATIONS
SUCCESSORS
PARALLEL LINEAGES

bestaan.

Coherentie komt niet uit uniformiteit.

Coherentie komt uit:

PROVENANCE
SCOPE
TIME
AUTHORITY
EVIDENCE
RECONCILIATION

Daarmee wordt HORTUS werkelijk een constitutionele ecologie.


---

