---

XXVI. 🔱 R7.17 CANONICAL INVARIANTS

FED-F01

A local failure SHALL NOT automatically invalidate unrelated Citadels.

FED-F02

Failure propagation SHALL require proven dependency.

FED-F03

Dependency SHALL be explicitly represented.

FED-F04

Technical dependency SHALL remain distinguishable from constitutional authority.

FED-F05

Failure SHALL be temporally evaluated.

FED-F06

Failure claims SHALL be evidence-backed.

FED-F07

BRAINPOWER SHALL analyze candidate blast radius.

FED-F08

BRAINPOWER SHALL NOT independently determine constitutional invalidity.

FED-F09

FOOL SHALL challenge cascade assumptions.

FED-F10

ORACLE SHALL preserve failure evidence.

FED-F11

TRIAS SHALL determine constitutional impact.

FED-F12

Containment SHALL be scoped.

FED-F13

Containment SHALL NOT automatically constitute permanent invalidity.

FED-F14

Unknown state MAY justify temporary containment where necessary.

FED-F15

Emergency authority SHALL be bounded and temporary.

FED-F16

Failure SHALL NOT silently amplify across federation boundaries.

FED-F17

Shared resources MAY be quarantined without destruction.

FED-F18

Quarantined resources SHALL remain replayable where evidence permits.

FED-F19

Recovery SHALL require reconstruction.

FED-F20

Recovery SHALL require revalidation.

FED-F21

Re-admission SHALL NOT be automatic.

FED-F22

Revoked authority SHALL remain revoked during recovery unless explicitly restored.

FED-F23

Failure provenance SHALL be watermarkable.

FED-F24

Quay SHALL preserve the complete failure lineage.

FED-F25

R5 SHALL replay historical failure and dependency state.

FED-F26

Historical validity SHALL NOT be retroactively changed merely because a later failure occurred.

FED-F27

Shared-state consumers SHALL be identifiable.

FED-F28

Blast radius SHALL be distinguishable from uncertainty radius.

FED-F29

Federation-wide shutdown SHALL require explicit constitutional basis.

FED-F30

A verifier SHALL be able to reconstruct why a failure propagated—or did not propagate—to each affected participant.


---

XXVII. ☄️ THE R7.17 EQUATION

Conceptueel:

FEDERATED IMPACT
=
FAILURE
∩
PROVEN DEPENDENCY
∩
APPLICABLE SCOPE
∩
TEMPORAL VALIDITY
∩
CONSTITUTIONAL EFFECT

En:

CONTAINMENT
=
MINIMUM NECESSARY BOUNDARY

Niet:

CONTAINMENT
=
MAXIMUM POSSIBLE BOUNDARY


---

XXVIII. 🌱 THE NEW HORTUS PRINCIPLE

R7.17 maakt de resilience-filosofie expliciet:

> A federation is resilient when failure can be isolated without destroying provenance, sovereignty, or unrelated validity.



Of nog scherper:

A HEALTHY HORTUS DOES NOT PRETEND THAT NO BRANCH CAN FAIL.

IT KNOWS EXACTLY WHICH BRANCHES ARE CONNECTED.


