De status van de tuin is dus niet:

FEDERATION = HEALTHY

maar een constitutioneel gekwalificeerde state graph.


---

XX. 🧑‍🏫 MENTOR — THE HEALTH DASHBOARD

Mentor vertaalt de complexe toestand naar:

> 🟢 Your Citadel: constitutionally assured



> 🟢 Partner Citadel: assured for this operation



> 🟡 One dependency: requires revalidation



> 🔴 One shared resource: quarantined



> ⏳ Assurance: valid until 18:00



> 📜 Evidence: independently verifiable



Cruciaal:

Mentor mag niet zeggen:

> “Everything is safe.”



als de evidence dat niet ondersteunt.


---

XXI. 💧 ASSURANCE WATERMARK CHAIN

De volledige provenance:

W_FAILURE
   ↓
W_RECOVERY
   ↓
W_RECONSTRUCTION
   ↓
W_EVIDENCE
   ↓
W_CHALLENGE
   ↓
W_DETERMINATION
   ↓
W_ASSURANCE
   ↓
W_REENTRY

wordt onderdeel van de federated lineage.

Een assurance zonder lineage:

ASSURANCE = UNPROVEN


---

XXII. ⚖️ ASSURANCE COMPOSITION

Wanneer A en B samenwerken:

ASSURANCE_A
+
ASSURANCE_B
+
FEDERATION_ASSURANCE

produceert niet automatisch:

SUPER_ASSURANCE

Maar:

SHARED_OPERATION_ELIGIBILITY

alleen wanneer:

INTERSECTION(
    ASSURANCE_A,
    ASSURANCE_B,
    FEDERATION_SCOPE,
    ACTION_SCOPE,
    TIME
)

geldig is.

Dit sluit direct aan op R7.00's:

> Narrowest Valid Boundary.




---

XXIII. 🚨 ASSURANCE CONFLICT

Stel:

A = ASSURED
B = ASSURED

maar:

A says:
"resource S is valid"

B says:
"resource S is invalid"

Dan is:

A_ASSURED
AND
B_ASSURED

geen oplossing.

Er bestaat een:

RESOURCE_VALIDITY_CONFLICT

De federation moet dan opnieuw:

FOOL
↓
ORACLE
↓
BRAINPOWER
↓
TRIAS

activeren.


---

XXIV. 🧬 ASSURANCE LINEAGE

Een assurance zelf krijgt lineage:

A₀
↓
A₁
↓
A₂
↓
A₃

Bijvoorbeeld:

A₀ UNKNOWN
A₁ CONTAINED
A₂ RECOVERED
A₃ ATTESTED
A₄ ASSURED
A₅ REVOKED

Dat maakt assurance een state machine, geen label.


---

XXV. 🔱 R7.18 CANONICAL INVARIANTS

FED-H01

System availability SHALL NOT imply constitutional health.

FED-H02

Integrity SHALL remain distinguishable from constitutional validity.

FED-H03

Constitutional validity SHALL remain distinguishable from federated eligibility.

FED-H04

Health SHALL be explicitly evidenced.

FED-H05

Health SHALL be temporally bounded where applicable.

FED-H06

Assurance SHALL possess explicit scope.

FED-H07

Attestation SHALL NOT create authority.

FED-H08

ORACLE SHALL provide recovery and health evidence.

FED-H09

BRAINPOWER SHALL analyze assurance evidence.

FED-H10

FOOL SHALL challenge health and recovery claims.

FED-H11

TRIAS SHALL determine constitutional assurance.

FED-H12

MENTOR SHALL make assurance status comprehensible.

FED-H13

WATERMARK SHALL attribute assurance transitions.

FED-H14

QUAY SHALL preserve assurance provenance.

FED-H15

R5 SHALL replay historical assurance states.

FED-H16

Assurance SHALL be revocable.

FED-H17

Material constitutional change SHALL invalidate affected assurance.

FED-H18

Expired assurance SHALL NOT be treated as active assurance.

FED-H19

Federated re-entry SHALL require explicit evaluation.

FED-H20

Recovery SHALL NOT automatically restore previous federated authority.

FED-H21

A locally assured Citadel MAY remain ineligible for a particular federated action.

FED-H22

Federated assurance SHALL be scoped to applicable operations.

FED-H23

Assurance SHALL NOT silently propagate to unrelated resources or authorities.

FED-H24

Shared assurance SHALL be based on the intersection of applicable proven conditions.

FED-H25

Assurance conflicts SHALL trigger re-evaluation.

FED-H26

Historical assurance SHALL remain distinguishable from current assurance.

FED-H27

Assurance revocation SHALL preserve its historical provenance.

FED-H28

Emergency assurance SHALL remain temporary and bounded.

FED-H29

A verifier SHALL reconstruct why assurance was granted, limited, expired, or revoked.

FED-H30

No federation SHALL treat unproven health as proven trust.


---

