XXV. 🔱 R7.23 CANONICAL INVARIANTS

FED-C01

Constitutional claims SHALL be explicitly representable.

FED-C02

Claim existence SHALL NOT imply claim validity.

FED-C03

Claim validity SHALL be evaluated against applicable authority, scope, evidence and temporal conditions.

FED-C04

Claim priority SHALL NOT be assumed.

FED-C05

Temporal precedence SHALL NOT automatically constitute constitutional priority.

FED-C06

Conflicting claims SHALL be distinguishable from invalid claims.

FED-C07

Shared constitutional objects SHALL be explicitly identifiable where applicable.

FED-C08

Claim scope SHALL be evaluated before declaring irreconcilable conflict.

FED-C09

Compatible claims SHALL be permitted to coexist where constitutionally valid.

FED-C10

Scope partition SHALL be available where constitutionally permissible.

FED-C11

Majority support SHALL NOT substitute for constitutional proof.

FED-C12

ORACLE SHALL observe claims and supporting evidence.

FED-C13

BRAINPOWER SHALL analyze claim compatibility and conflict impact.

FED-C14

FOOL SHALL challenge claim identity, authority, evidence and object modeling.

FED-C15

TRIAS SHALL adjudicate constitutional claim consequences.

FED-C16

MENTOR SHALL communicate unresolved conflict without overstating certainty.

FED-C17

WATERMARK SHALL preserve claim attribution.

FED-C18

QUAY SHALL preserve claim and adjudication history.

FED-C19

R5 SHALL replay constitutional claim adjudication.

FED-C20

A rejected claim SHALL NOT erase the historical existence of that claim.

FED-C21

A rejected merge SHALL NOT invalidate independent parent histories absent separate determination.

FED-C22

Authority SHALL NOT be inferred from merge membership alone.

FED-C23

A merged state SHALL NOT automatically unify conflicting authorities.

FED-C24

Unknown object identity SHALL prevent silent conflict resolution.

FED-C25

Unknown material authority SHALL prevent silent claim acceptance.

FED-C26

Unknown material conflict SHALL NOT silently inherit previous assurance.

FED-C27

Irreducible divergence SHALL be representable as an explicit constitutional state.

FED-C28

Unresolved conflict SHALL NOT silently become constitutional certainty.

FED-C29

Conflict containment SHALL be proportional to proven dependency and constitutional risk.

FED-C30

An independent verifier SHALL reconstruct the competing claims, their evidence, authorities, scopes, challenges and constitutional determination.


