XXII. 🔱 R7.24 CANONICAL INVARIANTS

FED-A01

Authority SHALL be distinguishable from jurisdiction.

FED-A02

Jurisdiction SHALL be distinguishable from execution right.

FED-A03

Valid authority SHALL NOT automatically imply unrestricted execution authority.

FED-A04

Jurisdiction SHALL be scoped.

FED-A05

Jurisdiction SHALL be temporally bounded where applicable.

FED-A06

Overlapping jurisdiction SHALL be explicitly detectable.

FED-A07

Authority collision SHALL be distinguishable from authority invalidity.

FED-A08

Execution order SHALL NOT create retroactive constitutional precedence.

FED-A09

Precedence SHALL require an explicit constitutional basis.

FED-A10

ORACLE SHALL observe authority and execution events.

FED-A11

BRAINPOWER SHALL analyze authority collision.

FED-A12

FOOL SHALL challenge jurisdiction, ordering and concurrency assumptions.

FED-A13

TRIAS SHALL determine constitutional execution relationships.

FED-A14

TRIAS SHALL NOT itself constitute execution.

FED-A15

MENTOR SHALL expose execution status without overstating certainty.

FED-A16

WATERMARK SHALL attribute execution.

FED-A17

QUAY SHALL preserve execution lineage.

FED-A18

R5 SHALL replay authority collision and execution determination.

FED-A19

Compatible authorities MAY execute concurrently where constitutionally permitted.

FED-A20

Order-dependent actions SHALL require explicit ordering.

FED-A21

Joint constitutional operations SHALL support joint authorization where required.

FED-A22

Mutually exclusive execution SHALL NOT occur concurrently.

FED-A23

Unknown high-risk execution relationships SHALL fail closed or enter hold.

FED-A24

Low-risk observational activity MAY continue where constitutionally permitted.

FED-A25

Partial execution SHALL be explicitly represented.

FED-A26

Atomicity requirements SHALL be explicit for constitutionally coupled operations.

FED-A27

A blocked execution attempt SHALL remain historically observable.

FED-A28

Authority collision SHALL be contained to the smallest proven affected domain.

FED-A29

Federation-wide containment SHALL require proven dependency or constitutional rule.

FED-A30

An independent verifier SHALL reconstruct the authority, jurisdiction, collision, determination, execution and resulting state.


