FED-C13

QUAY SHALL preserve distributed event lineage.

FED-C14

R5 SHALL reconstruct causal and temporal determinations.

FED-C15

Clock drift SHALL be representable where relevant.

FED-C16

Unknown ordering SHALL remain explicitly unknown.

FED-C17

Unknown causality SHALL remain explicitly unknown.

FED-C18

Concurrent events MAY coexist where constitutional constraints permit.

FED-C19

A partial order SHALL be preferred over an unproven total order.

FED-C20

Constitutional state SHALL remain compatible with all proven causal constraints.

FED-C21

Contradictory causal evidence SHALL trigger constitutional review.

FED-C22

Temporal evidence SHALL be independently verifiable where constitutionally relevant.

FED-C23

A local clock SHALL NOT acquire constitutional authority merely by being earlier.

FED-C24

Federation-wide ordering SHALL require federation-level evidence or constitutional rule.

FED-C25

Concurrent execution SHALL NOT be treated as sequential execution without proof.

FED-C26

State reconstruction SHALL preserve causal uncertainty.

FED-C27

A missing global clock SHALL NOT imply missing constitutional truth.

FED-C28

A causal graph SHALL remain reconstructible from preserved evidence.

FED-C29

Containment SHALL follow proven dependency, not temporal proximity.

FED-C30

An independent verifier SHALL determine whether event order, causality and resulting consistency are proven, unproven or contradicted.


